#. Crypto invoice, Bitcoin only: the network to send on, shown with the address. Bitcoin sent on another network is not credited to this payment. The Bitcoin counterpart of usdc_solana_network_only. Bitcoin is a product name.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_bitcoin_network_only"
msgid "Send only Bitcoin on the Bitcoin network to this address. Bitcoin sent on any other network won't be credited."
msgstr "Envoyez uniquement du Bitcoin sur le réseau Bitcoin à cette adresse. Le Bitcoin envoyé sur un autre réseau ne sera pas crédité."

#. Crypto invoice: shown briefly in place of Copy after the amount or the address was copied.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_copied"
msgid "Copied"
msgstr "Copié"

#. Crypto invoice: button that copies the amount or the address beside it to the clipboard. Apple shows this text through the copy key, which has the same source.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_copy"
msgid "Copy"
msgstr "Copier"

#. Crypto invoice: button that copies the receiving address to the clipboard, where the amount has its own copy button too (crypto_invoice_copy_amount), as on a TAO invoice. It shows Copied (crypto_invoice_copied) for a moment after a tap.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_copy_address"
msgid "Copy address"
msgstr "Copier l’adresse"

#. Crypto invoice: button that copies the exact amount to send (the number, without the ticker) to the clipboard, beside Copy address (crypto_invoice_copy_address), as on a TAO invoice. It shows Copied (crypto_invoice_copied) for a moment after a tap.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_copy_amount"
msgid "Copy amount"
msgstr "Copier le montant"

#. Crypto invoice, ETH only: the network to send on, shown with the address. The same address exists on other networks that carry ETH, such as Base and Arbitrum (network names, never translated), and ETH sent there, like any token sent to the address, is not credited to this payment. Use the same words for mainnet as crypto_network_eth. Ethereum and ETH are product names.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_eth_network_only"
msgid "Send only ETH on Ethereum mainnet to this address. Tokens and ETH on other networks, such as Base or Arbitrum, won't be credited."
msgstr "Envoyez uniquement de l’ETH sur le réseau principal Ethereum à cette adresse. Les jetons et l’ETH d’autres réseaux, comme Base ou Arbitrum, ne seront pas crédités."

#. Crypto invoice: countdown under the amount. The amount of the coin is quoted at the current exchange rate and held for a limited time. {time} is the time left as minutes and seconds (m:ss, e.g. 29:59).
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_expires_in"
msgid "Quote expires in {}"
msgstr "La cotation expire dans {}"

#. Crypto invoice, USDC only: the label above the payment's reference (memo). A payer who types the transfer into a wallet by hand must include it; paying from the QR code or Open in wallet fills it in.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_memo"
msgid "Memo, if you send by hand"
msgstr "Mémo, si vous envoyez manuellement"

#. Crypto invoice: button that opens the payment request (address and exact amount) in a wallet app on this device.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_open_wallet"
msgid "Open in wallet"
msgstr "Ouvrir dans le portefeuille"

#. Crypto invoice: link that closes the invoice and goes back to the payment methods.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_pay_another_way"
msgid "Pay another way"
msgstr "Payer autrement"

#. Crypto invoice: shown when the quote's time ran out before any payment arrived. Refreshing keeps the same address and changes only the amount.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_quote_expired"
msgid "This quote expired. Refresh it for a new amount."
msgstr "Cette cotation a expiré. Actualisez-la pour obtenir un nouveau montant."

#. Crypto invoice: button shown once the quote has expired. It gets a new amount of the coin at the current exchange rate, for the same address.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_refresh_quote"
msgid "Refresh quote"
msgstr "Actualiser la cotation"

#. Crypto invoice: shown when a payment arrived but was short of the amount. {amount} is what is still to send, with the coin's ticker (e.g. 0.0012 XMR).
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_remaining"
msgid "{} more to send"
msgstr "Encore {} à envoyer"

#. Crypto invoice: the label above the exact amount of the coin to send (e.g. 0.072387 XMR), which has a copy button.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_send_exactly"
msgid "Send exactly"
msgstr "Envoyez exactement"

#. Crypto invoice for a coin with no payment link (TAO): the instruction above the exact amount and the receiving address, which each have their own copy button (crypto_invoice_copy_amount, crypto_invoice_copy_address). It stands where other coins show Open in wallet. Exactly: the payer must send this amount, no more and no less.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_send_exactly_to_address"
msgid "Send exactly this amount to this address."
msgstr "Envoyez exactement ce montant à cette adresse."

#. Crypto invoice, SOL only: the coin to send, shown with the address. Only SOL itself counts: tokens sent to the address, USDC among them, are not credited to this payment (USDC is paid on its own tab, USDC on Solana). Solana, SOL and USDC are product names.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_sol_network_only"
msgid "Send only SOL on the Solana network to this address. Tokens, including USDC, won't be credited."
msgstr "Envoyez uniquement des SOL sur le réseau Solana à cette adresse. Les jetons, y compris les USDC, ne seront pas crédités."

#. Crypto invoice, TAO only: the network to send on, shown with the address. TAO sent on another network is not credited to this payment. The TAO counterpart of usdc_solana_network_only. Bittensor and TAO are product names.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_tao_network_only"
msgid "Send only TAO on the Bittensor network to this address. TAO sent on any other network won't be credited."
msgstr "Envoyez uniquement des TAO sur le réseau Bittensor à cette adresse. Les TAO envoyés sur un autre réseau ne seront pas crédités."

#. Crypto invoice, TAO only: why it has no Open in wallet button, and what its QR code holds. TAO has no payment link (a link or QR code that fills in both the address and the amount, as other coins have), so the QR code carries the address alone and the payer enters the exact amount by hand. TAO is a product name.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_tao_no_payment_link"
msgid "TAO has no payment link, so this QR code holds only the address. Enter the exact amount in your wallet."
msgstr "Le TAO n’a pas de lien de paiement : ce code QR ne contient donc que l’adresse. Saisissez le montant exact dans votre portefeuille."

#. Crypto invoice: the label above the receiving address, which has a copy button.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_to_address"
msgid "To this address"
msgstr "À cette adresse"

#. Crypto invoice: shown when an invoice can't be started or its quote refreshed because the coin can't be quoted right now. {method} is the coin's name: USDC, Zcash, Monero, TAO, Bitcoin, ETH or SOL (product names, never translated).
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_unavailable"
msgid "Paying with {} is temporarily unavailable. Try again later, or pay another way."
msgstr "Le paiement en {} est temporairement indisponible. Réessayez plus tard ou payez autrement."

#. Crypto invoice: wallet apps known to pay this coin. {wallets} is a comma-separated list of wallet app names (e.g. Cake, Feather, Monerujo), which are never translated.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_wallets"
msgid "Wallets that work: {}"
msgstr "Portefeuilles compatibles : {}"

#. Crypto invoice, Zcash only: warning that exchange accounts cannot pay a shielded address, so the payer must send from a wallet that supports shielded Zcash addresses. Coinbase and Robinhood are company names. Use the same word for shielded as in crypto_network_zcash.
msgctxt "crypto_invoice_zcash_exchange_note"
msgid "Exchanges such as Coinbase and Robinhood can't send to this shielded address. Send from a shielded wallet."
msgstr "Les plateformes d’échange comme Coinbase et Robinhood ne peuvent pas envoyer vers cette adresse blindée. Envoyez depuis un portefeuille compatible avec les adresses blindées."

#. The network a Bitcoin payment is sent on: the Bitcoin invoice's first line, and the line under Bitcoin in the More coins list, so the payer picks the right network in the wallet or the exchange. Bitcoin is a product name.
msgctxt "crypto_network_bitcoin"
msgid "Bitcoin network"
msgstr "Réseau Bitcoin"

#. The network an ETH payment is sent on: the ETH invoice's first line, and the line under ETH in the More coins list. Mainnet is Ethereum's main network, as opposed to its test networks and to other networks that carry ETH, such as Base and Arbitrum (ETH sent there is not credited). Use the same words for mainnet as crypto_invoice_eth_network_only. Ethereum is a product name.
msgctxt "crypto_network_eth"
msgid "Ethereum mainnet"
msgstr "Réseau principal Ethereum"

#. Crypto invoice: its first line, naming the coin (Monero has a single network). A product name: never translated. Apple shows this text through pay_method_monero, which has the same source.
msgctxt "crypto_network_monero"
msgid "Monero"
msgstr "Monero"

#. The network a SOL payment is sent on: the SOL invoice's first line, and the line under SOL in the More coins list. Native SOL is the Solana network's own coin, as opposed to the tokens on Solana such as USDC, which has its own tab. Solana and SOL are product names.
msgctxt "crypto_network_sol"
msgid "Solana (native SOL)"
msgstr "Solana (SOL natif)"

#. The network a TAO payment is sent on: the TAO invoice's first line, and the line under TAO in the More coins list, so the payer picks the right network in the wallet or the exchange. Bittensor is a product name.
msgctxt "crypto_network_tao"
msgid "Bittensor network"
msgstr "Réseau Bittensor"

#. Crypto invoice: its first line, naming the coin and the network to send it on, so the payer picks the right chain in the wallet (USDC sent on another chain is lost). On apple it also labels the USDC tab of the payment method row (pay_method_usdc_solana, the same text), so keep it short enough for a tab.
msgctxt "crypto_network_usdc"
msgid "USDC on Solana"
msgstr "USDC sur Solana"

#. Crypto invoice: its first line, naming the coin and saying the receiving address is a shielded (private) Zcash address. Use the word Zcash wallets in the language use for shielded; the same word appears in the Zcash exchange note.
msgctxt "crypto_network_zcash"
msgid "Zcash, shielded"
msgstr "Zcash, blindé"

#. The buy button while a coin is the chosen payment method. {method} is the sdk's label for the coin, as the method row or the More coins list shows it, for example USDC on Solana, Zcash, Monero, TAO, Bitcoin, ETH or SOL (product names, never translated). A word that changes with the name's last sound (Korean 로/으로) takes the form that fits every name.
msgctxt "crypto_pay_button"
msgid "Pay with {}"
msgstr "Payer en {}"

#. Account screen and plan area: the label of the row or banner that reopens a crypto invoice (in any coin) saved on this device and not paid yet. Tapping it opens the invoice.
msgctxt "crypto_payment_in_progress"
msgid "Payment in progress"
msgstr "Paiement en cours"

#. Crypto invoice status: the full payment arrived and is collecting block confirmations. {count} is the confirmations so far and {required} the number needed before the purchase is credited (e.g. 3 of 10). Numbers only follow, so no plural forms.
msgctxt "crypto_status_confirming"
msgid "Confirming: {0} of {1}"
msgstr "Confirmation : {0} sur {1}"

#. Crypto invoice status: the payment is confirmed and the plan or the data has been credited.
msgctxt "crypto_status_paid"
msgid "Paid. Thank you!"
msgstr "Payé. Merci !"

#. Crypto invoice status: a payment needs a person to review it (it was short when the quote expired, a second payment arrived, or a payment dropped off the chain). Nothing is lost; support settles it.
msgctxt "crypto_status_review"
msgid "We received a payment that needs a manual check. Contact support and we'll sort it out."
msgstr "Nous avons reçu un paiement qui nécessite une vérification manuelle. Contactez l’assistance et nous réglerons le problème."

#. Crypto invoice status: a payment has appeared on the network but is not confirmed yet, or is not the full amount yet. Nothing has been credited.
msgctxt "crypto_status_seen"
msgid "Payment seen"
msgstr "Paiement détecté"

#. Crypto invoice status: no payment has arrived yet.
msgctxt "crypto_status_waiting"
msgid "Waiting for your payment"
msgstr "En attente de votre paiement"

#. In-app notice once a year of Pro paid once in crypto (it never auto-renews) has ended and its 30-day grace period has begun. {date} is the last day of the grace period, formatted by the app for the reader's locale. Renew by = no later than.
msgctxt "crypto_term_ended_notice"
msgid "Your paid year of Pro has ended. Renew by {} to keep Pro."
msgstr "Votre année de Pro payée est terminée. Renouvelez d’ici le {} pour conserver Pro."

#. Button on the notice that a crypto-paid year of Pro has ended: opens the plan picker to pay for another year.
msgctxt "crypto_term_renew"
msgid "Renew"
msgstr "Renouveler"

#. A label showing the current network API and connect URLs.
msgctxt "current_api_n"
msgid "Current API: {}"
msgstr "API actuelle : {}"

#. A label displaying the current connect URL.
msgctxt "current_connect_n"
msgid "Current connect: {}"
msgstr "Connexion actuelle : {}"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "current_network_referral"
msgid "Current network referral"
msgstr "Réseau de parrainage actuel"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "current_ranking"
msgid "Current Ranking"
msgstr "Classement actuel"

#. Used in Main/Account/Settings/UpdateReferralNetworkSheet/UpdateReferralNetworkSheet.swift.
msgctxt "current_referral_network"
msgid "Current referral network"
msgstr "Réseau de parrainage actuel"

#. Title of a section in the connect drawer that shows the custom dns settings.
msgctxt "custom_dns"
msgid "Custom DNS"
msgstr "DNS personnalisé"

#. Connect error: the system service could not check whether the account may connect.
msgctxt "daemon_auth_check_failed"
msgid "The URnetwork system service could not check whether this account is allowed to connect, so it did not connect. Try again."
msgstr "Le service système URnetwork n’a pas pu vérifier si ce compte est autorisé à se connecter, il ne s’est donc pas connecté. Réessayez."

#. Connect error: the device policy does not allow this account to connect.
msgctxt "daemon_auth_denied"
msgid "This device's policy does not allow this account to connect through URnetwork. An administrator can change that."
msgstr "La politique de cet appareil n’autorise pas ce compte à se connecter via URnetwork. Un administrateur peut changer cela."

#. Connect error: administrator permission is needed from this session.
msgctxt "daemon_auth_required"
msgid "Connecting from this session needs administrator permission. Press Connect again to be asked, or use the session at this device's screen."
msgstr "Se connecter depuis cette session nécessite une autorisation d’administrateur. Appuyez de nouveau sur Connecter pour qu’elle vous soit demandée, ou utilisez la session à l’écran de cet appareil."

#. Connect error: the permission request was not answered.
msgctxt "daemon_auth_timeout"
msgid "The permission request was not answered, so nothing was connected. Press Connect to try again."
msgstr "La demande d’autorisation est restée sans réponse, rien n’a donc été connecté. Appuyez sur Connecter pour réessayer."

#. Connect error: no polkit service, the daemon falls back to the urnetwork group.
msgctxt "daemon_auth_unavailable"
msgid "This device has no polkit authorization service, so the URnetwork system service falls back to the 'urnetwork' group. Add your user to it and sign out and back in."
msgstr "Cet appareil n’a pas de service d’autorisation polkit, le service système URnetwork se rabat donc sur le groupe 'urnetwork'. Ajoutez-y votre utilisateur, puis déconnectez-vous et reconnectez-vous."

#. Linux notice when an older system service refuses the app's user. 'urnetwork' is the literal Linux group name; keep it as is.
msgctxt "daemon_legacy_group_auth"
msgid "The URnetwork system service on this device is an older version that still requires group membership. Update the service, or add your user to the 'urnetwork' group and sign out and back in."
msgstr "Le service système URnetwork de cet appareil est une ancienne version qui exige encore l’appartenance à un groupe. Mettez à jour le service, ou ajoutez votre utilisateur au groupe 'urnetwork', puis déconnectez-vous de votre session et reconnectez-vous."

#. Error: the system service did not answer.
msgctxt "daemon_no_answer"
msgid "The URnetwork system service did not answer."
msgstr "Le service système URnetwork n’a pas répondu."

#. Linux notice when the app cannot reach the URnetwork system service for an unexpected reason.
msgctxt "daemon_not_reachable"
msgid "The URnetwork system service could not be reached."
msgstr "Le service système URnetwork est injoignable."

#. Shown on the linux home screen when the app and the urnetworkd system service carry different URnetwork SDK builds (they update on independent schedules and must match exactly). The fix is updating both to the same release.
msgctxt "daemon_sdk_mismatch"
msgid "The app and the URnetwork system service are different builds. Update both to the same version."
msgstr "L'application et le service système URnetwork sont des builds différents. Mettez les deux à jour vers la même version."

#. Linux notice when the app cannot reach the URnetwork system service because the service restarted under a sandboxed (Flatpak) app.
msgctxt "daemon_stale_sandbox_mount"
msgid "The URnetwork system service restarted while this app was open. Close the app and open it again to reconnect to it."
msgstr "Le service système URnetwork a redémarré pendant que cette application était ouverte. Fermez l’application et rouvrez-la pour vous y reconnecter."

#. Shown on the linux home screen when the installed urnetworkd system service speaks an older control protocol than this app supports. Distinct from daemon_unreachable by contract; the fix is updating the service, not the app.
msgctxt "daemon_too_old"
msgid "The URnetwork system service is out of date. Update it to connect."
msgstr "Le service système URnetwork n'est pas à jour. Mettez-le à jour pour vous connecter."

#. Connect error: another user on the device holds the tunnel.
msgctxt "daemon_tunnel_owned_by_other_user"
msgid "Another user on this device is connected through URnetwork. Disconnect it from their session, or take it over with administrator permission."
msgstr "Un autre utilisateur de cet appareil est connecté via URnetwork. Déconnectez-le depuis sa session, ou reprenez la connexion avec une autorisation d’administrateur."

#. Shown on the linux home screen when the privileged urnetworkd system service cannot be reached over its control socket (not installed, not running, or the user lacks access). Distinct from daemon_too_old by contract.
msgctxt "daemon_unreachable"
msgid "The URnetwork system service is not running. Install or start it, then try again."
msgstr "Le service système URnetwork n'est pas en cours d'exécution. Installez-le ou démarrez-le, puis réessayez."

#. Key of the daily data balance row on the Account page, in the data info sheet and under the usage bar: a label beside its right-aligned value, so it carries no colon.
msgctxt "daily_data_balance"
msgid "Daily Data Balance"
msgstr "Solde de données quotidien"

#. Guidance for someone who has no code yet. Deliberately PLAIN TEXT with no link and no button: app store rules forbid steering a user to an external purchase, but nothing stops us saying where codes come from. Without this, the sheet asks for a code and gives no way to obtain one.
msgctxt "daily_data_balance_label"
msgid "Daily Data Balance:"
msgstr "Solde de données quotidien :"

#. Used in Main/Account/Settings/SettingsForm-iOS.swift.
msgctxt "danger"
msgid "Danger"
msgstr "Danger"

#. Guidance for someone who has no code yet. Deliberately PLAIN TEXT with no link and no button: app store rules forbid steering a user to an external purchase, but nothing stops us saying where codes come from. Without this, the sheet asks for a code and gives no way to obtain one.
msgctxt "data"
msgid "Data"
msgstr "Données"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "data_bar_explanation"
msgid "This bar in the app shows you how much free data you are earning from your provider. You can check in any time and adjust your settings to maximize your earnings."
msgstr "Cette barre dans l’application vous montre combien de données gratuites vous gagnez auprès de votre fournisseur. Vous pouvez vérifier à tout moment et ajuster vos paramètres pour maximiser vos gains."

#. "About your data" sheet: explains the Available part of the usage bar, shown under the Available amount.
msgctxt "data_info_available"
msgid "Data you can still use."
msgstr "Données que vous pouvez encore utiliser."

#. "About your data" sheet: explains the Pending part of the usage bar, shown under the Pending amount. Pending is balance held (escrowed) by the user's open connections; the unused part is returned when they close. Do not add a time promise.
msgctxt "data_info_pending"
msgid "Data reserved for your open connections. What they don't use is returned when they close."
msgstr "Données réservées à vos connexions ouvertes. Ce qu’elles n’utilisent pas vous est rendu à leur fermeture."

#. "About your data" sheet: when the free daily data is granted again. {time} is the time left until the next 00:00 UTC as a compact duration (e.g. 5h 12m). Keep 00:00 UTC as is. Every account gets the free daily data, Pro accounts included. Which accounts see this line is up to each app (today: only accounts without Pro).
msgctxt "data_info_refresh_at"
msgid "Free data refreshes daily at 00:00 UTC (in {})."
msgstr "Les données gratuites sont renouvelées chaque jour à 00:00 UTC (dans {})."

#. Title of the "About your data" sheet, opened from the info button next to the daily data balance in the usage bar and from the Why? link under an out-of-balance notice. Also the info button's accessibility label.
msgctxt "data_info_title"
msgid "About your data"
msgstr "À propos de vos données"

#. "About your data" sheet: explains the Used part of the usage bar, shown under the Used amount.
msgctxt "data_info_used"
msgid "Data you've used so far."
msgstr "Données que vous avez utilisées jusqu’à présent."

#. Link under the out-of-balance notice that opens the "About your data" sheet.
msgctxt "data_info_why"
msgid "Why?"
msgstr "Pourquoi ?"

#. Alert body shown in the app and in a local notification when a paying account is refused at a data limit while the tunnel is capturing traffic. Connect stays requested and the VPN keeps holding traffic until the limit allows more data or the user disconnects. The paying counterpart of insufficient_balance_held_notice, with no upgrade to offer.
msgctxt "data_limit_held_notice"
msgid "Your traffic is held in the tunnel until more data is available or you disconnect."
msgstr "Votre trafic est retenu dans le tunnel jusqu’à ce que davantage de données soient disponibles ou que vous vous déconnectiez."

#. Alert title and status line on the connect screen, and the title of a local notification, when the server refuses a paying account's connection because a data limit was reached (a per-device data cap or the plan's data), not because the account has no balance. Short.
msgctxt "data_limit_reached"
msgid "Data limit reached"
msgstr "Limite de données atteinte"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "data_usage"
msgid "Data usage"
msgstr "Utilisation des données"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "date_payout"
msgid "{} Payout"
msgstr "Paiement du {}"

#. Compact relative-time label with an abbreviated days unit ("3d ago"), shown by the windows and linux relative-time formatters (the Sessions screen's Last used) for events a day to 7 days old; older events show a date. The argument is the elapsed days. Not a plural: the abbreviated unit does not inflect, but the word order and the unit abbreviation localize.
msgctxt "days_ago_abbrev"
msgid "{}d ago"
msgstr "il y a {} j"

#. Onboarding data page: the daily free allowance, formatted from the server's balance (pro.yml free.data per data_period).
msgctxt "default_daily_data"
msgid "By default, you get {} every day."
msgstr "Par défaut, vous recevez {} chaque jour."

#. Generic default choice label, e.g. the app split rule combo state meaning no rule.
msgctxt "default_option"
msgid "Default"
msgstr "Par défaut"

#. Delete button label. Apple: Main/Account/BlockedLocations/BlockedLocationsView.swift. Android: the swipe-to-reveal delete button label (SwipeToRevealRow).
msgctxt "delete"
msgid "Delete"
msgstr "Supprimer"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "delete_account"
msgid "Delete Account"
msgstr "Supprimer le compte"

#. Used in Main/Account/Settings/SettingsForm-iOS.swift.
msgctxt "delete_account_2"
msgid "Delete account"
msgstr "Supprimer le compte"

#. Delete account dialog: asks the user to type the network name back before the delete button enables. {network} is the account's network name.
msgctxt "delete_account_type_network_name"
msgid "Type {} to confirm."
msgstr "Saisissez {} pour confirmer."

#. Developer page: report line when the SDK refused a requested action.
msgctxt "dev_action_declined"
msgid "No change: the SDK declined that action."
msgstr "Aucun changement : le SDK a refusé cette action."

#. Developer page: note that the action buttons only request changes.
msgctxt "dev_actions_are_requests"
msgid "Actions are requests: confirm them in the measurements and exit rows, which refresh underneath."
msgstr "Les actions sont des demandes : vérifiez leur effet dans les mesures et les lignes de sorties, qui s’actualisent en dessous."

#. Developer tools: maximum original connection creation age for healthy ordinary-flow affinity, edited as a duration.
msgctxt "dev_affinity_max_time"
msgid "Maximum affinity age"
msgstr "Âge maximal de l’affinité"

#. Developer tools: strict healthy-donor age cap, disabled values, default and unaffected existing connections/pins.
msgctxt "dev_affinity_max_time_detail"
msgid "For ordinary new connections, reuse only a healthy IP/domain exit while the original connection's age since creation is below this limit. Default: 1 minute. Zero or negative disables reuse. Warned or unhealthy exits always race. Existing connections and explicit pins are unchanged."
msgstr "Pour les nouvelles connexions ordinaires, réutilise uniquement une sortie IP/domaine saine si le temps écoulé depuis la création de la connexion d’origine est inférieur à cette limite. Valeur par défaut : 1 minute. Zéro ou une valeur négative désactive la réutilisation. Une sortie avertie ou défaillante déclenche toujours une course. Les connexions existantes et les épinglages explicites ne changent pas."

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): performance-aware affinity control label.
msgctxt "dev_affinity_performance"
msgid "Performance-aware affinity"
msgstr "Affinité selon les performances"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the performance-aware affinity control.
msgctxt "dev_affinity_performance_detail"
msgid "Weight new TLS races by each provider's peak acknowledged-byte rate relative to its advertised bandwidth. Within the affinity age limit, low measured donors yield to the race. Existing connections and explicit pins stay fixed"
msgstr "Pondère les nouvelles courses TLS selon le débit maximal d’octets acquittés de chaque fournisseur par rapport à sa bande passante annoncée. Dans la limite d’âge de l’affinité, les fournisseurs peu performants cèdent à la course. Les connexions existantes et les épinglages explicites restent fixes"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): affinity sticky control label.
msgctxt "dev_affinity_sticky"
msgid "Sticky site affinity"
msgstr "Affinité persistante par site"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'affinity sticky' control.
msgctxt "dev_affinity_sticky_detail"
msgid "A site's new connections stay on the exit its earlier ones already use, even past the flow cap, so a busy site keeps one egress IP. The cap still limits which exits collect new sites. Off restores the strict cap"
msgstr "Les nouvelles connexions d’un site restent sur la sortie que ses connexions précédentes utilisent déjà, même au-delà du plafond de flux, pour qu’un site chargé garde une seule IP de sortie. Le plafond limite toujours les sorties qui accueillent de nouveaux sites. Désactivé rétablit le plafond strict"

#. Developer page: what a setting's 0 means when it probes every host ('Probe hosts per pass').
msgctxt "dev_all"
msgid "All"
msgstr "Tous"

#. Developer page: label of the app version row.
msgctxt "dev_app_version"
msgid "App version"
msgstr "Version de l’application"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): behaviour control label.
msgctxt "dev_behaviour"
msgid "Behaviour"
msgstr "Comportement"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): blackhole receive control label.
msgctxt "dev_blackhole_receive"
msgid "Keep quiet providers longer"
msgstr "Garder plus longtemps les fournisseurs silencieux"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'blackhole receive' control.
msgctxt "dev_blackhole_receive_detail"
msgid "How long a provider still acknowledging traffic may return nothing before it is dropped. Off keeps them until they stop acknowledging"
msgstr "Combien de temps un fournisseur qui acquitte encore le trafic peut ne rien renvoyer avant d’être écarté. Désactivé les garde jusqu’à ce qu’ils cessent d’acquitter"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): blast radius control label.
msgctxt "dev_blast_radius"
msgid "Blast radius"
msgstr "Rayon d’impact"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'blast radius' control.
msgctxt "dev_blast_radius_detail"
msgid "Connections lost per provider failure. Lower is better"
msgstr "Connexions perdues par panne de fournisseur. Plus c’est bas, mieux c’est"

#. Developer tools screen: formatted value readout for 'blast radius'.
msgctxt "dev_blast_radius_value"
msgid "{} per failure"
msgstr "{} par panne"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): busy probe control label.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probe"
msgid "Probe stalled exits before dropping"
msgstr "Sonder les sorties figées avant de les écarter"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): busy probe budget control label.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probe_budget"
msgid "Busy probe wait"
msgstr "Attente de la sonde d’occupation"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'busy probe budget' control.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probe_budget_detail"
msgid "How long the stall probe waits for an answer before convicting. Off derives half the stall bar"
msgstr "Combien de temps la sonde de blocage attend une réponse avant de condamner. Désactivé utilise la moitié du seuil de blocage"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'busy probe' control.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probe_detail"
msgid "When an exit stalls, ping it once before convicting. A congested but alive exit answers and keeps its flows; a dead one is still dropped. Off convicts on the stall bar"
msgstr "Quand une sortie se fige, elle reçoit un ping avant d’être condamnée. Une sortie congestionnée mais vivante répond et garde ses flux ; une sortie morte est quand même écartée. Désactivé condamne au seuil de blocage"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Busy probe wait' setting.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probe_wait"
msgid "Busy probe wait"
msgstr "Attente de la sonde d’occupation"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Busy probe wait' setting.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probe_wait_detail"
msgid "How long the stall probe waits for an answer before convicting, in ms. Off derives half the stall bar"
msgstr "Combien de temps la sonde de blocage attend une réponse avant de condamner, en ms. Désactivé utilise la moitié du seuil de blocage"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): busy probes control label.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probes"
msgid "Busy probes"
msgstr "Sondes d’occupation"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'busy probes' control.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probes_detail"
msgid "Liveness pings fired at stalled exits; acquitted ones answered and were kept, the removals the probe prevented"
msgstr "Pings de vie envoyés aux sorties figées ; les acquittées ont répondu et ont été gardées — les retraits que la sonde a évités"

#. Developer tools screen: formatted value readout for 'busy probes'.
msgctxt "dev_busy_probes_value"
msgid "{0} sent / {1} acquitted"
msgstr "{0} envoyées / {1} acquittées"

#. Developer page: button that checks for a new release now. Linux Settings > General: the title of the row whose button does the same.
msgctxt "dev_check_updates"
msgid "Check for updates"
msgstr "Rechercher des mises à jour"

#. Developer tools screen: action for choosing individual log files to export.
msgctxt "dev_choose_logs"
msgid "Choose logs…"
msgstr "Choisir des journaux…"

#. Developer tools screen: action that deletes the diagnostics log files without touching local state, preferences or rules.
msgctxt "dev_clear_logs"
msgid "Clear logs"
msgstr "Effacer les journaux"

#. Developer tools screen: the clear-logs action's label while it runs.
msgctxt "dev_clearing_logs"
msgid "Clearing logs…"
msgstr "Effacement des journaux…"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): cluster affinity control label.
msgctxt "dev_cluster_affinity"
msgid "Group IPs by site"
msgstr "Regrouper les IP par site"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'cluster affinity' control.
msgctxt "dev_cluster_affinity_detail"
msgid "Keeps a site on one exit when its hostname is not visible"
msgstr "Garde un site sur une seule sortie quand son nom d’hôte n’est pas visible"

#. Developer page: table column header for the per-row action buttons.
msgctxt "dev_col_actions"
msgid "Actions"
msgstr "Actions"

#. Developer page: table column header for the connect timing.
msgctxt "dev_col_connect"
msgid "Connect"
msgstr "Connexion"

#. Developer page: table column header for a destination host.
msgctxt "dev_col_destination"
msgid "Destination"
msgstr "Destination"

#. Developer page: table column header for the DNS timing. A protocol name; never translated.
msgctxt "dev_col_dns"
msgid "DNS"
msgstr "DNS"

#. Developer page: table column header for the exit a flow uses.
msgctxt "dev_col_exit"
msgid "Exit"
msgstr "Sortie"

#. Developer page: table column header for the number of failed dials.
msgctxt "dev_col_failed_dials"
msgid "Failed dials"
msgstr "Échecs de connexion"

#. Developer page: table column header for the number of flows.
msgctxt "dev_col_flows"
msgid "Flows"
msgstr "Flux"

#. Developer page: table column header for the probe kind.
msgctxt "dev_col_kind"
msgid "Kind"
msgstr "Type"

#. Developer page: table column header for a probe outcome.
msgctxt "dev_col_outcome"
msgid "Outcome"
msgstr "Résultat"

#. Developer page: table column header for an exit state.
msgctxt "dev_col_state"
msgid "State"
msgstr "État"

#. Developer page: table column header for a probe target.
msgctxt "dev_col_target"
msgid "Target"
msgstr "Cible"

#. Developer page: table column header for an exit tier.
msgctxt "dev_col_tier"
msgid "Tier"
msgstr "Niveau"

#. Developer page: table column header for the total timing.
msgctxt "dev_col_total"
msgid "Total"
msgstr "Total"

#. Developer page: table column header for time to first byte. The metric's standard abbreviation; never translated.
msgctxt "dev_col_ttfb"
msgid "TTFB"
msgstr "TTFB"

#. Developer page: table column header for the measurement window.
msgctxt "dev_col_window"
msgid "Window"
msgstr "Fenêtre"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): comparative connect control label.
msgctxt "dev_comparative_connect"
msgid "Cut dead connects early"
msgstr "Couper tôt les connexions mortes"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'comparative connect' control.
msgctxt "dev_comparative_connect_detail"
msgid "Drop an exit that has established nothing sooner when two sibling exits are receiving. Off waits the full 30s connect bar"
msgstr "Écarte plus tôt une sortie qui n’a rien établi quand deux sorties sœurs reçoivent. Désactivé attend le seuil de connexion complet de 30 s"

#. Developer page (Apple): note shown while disconnected.
msgctxt "dev_connect_for_live_tools"
msgid "Connect to use the live connection tools. Diagnostics below work either way."
msgstr "Connectez-vous pour utiliser les outils de la connexion en cours. Les diagnostics ci-dessous fonctionnent dans tous les cas."

#. Developer page: label of the 'Corroborate silent exits' setting.
msgctxt "dev_corroborate_silent_exits"
msgid "Corroborate silent exits"
msgstr "Corroborer les sorties silencieuses"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Corroborate silent exits' setting.
msgctxt "dev_corroborate_silent_exits_detail"
msgid "How many distinct destinations must be silent before an exit is convicted on no-receive, so one dead site cannot remove a working exit"
msgstr "Combien de destinations distinctes doivent rester silencieuses avant qu’une sortie soit condamnée pour absence de réception, pour qu’un seul site en panne ne puisse pas retirer une sortie qui fonctionne"

#. Developer page: suffix after a count of affected flows.
msgctxt "dev_count_affected"
msgid "affected"
msgstr "concernés"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Cut dead connects early' setting.
msgctxt "dev_cut_dead_connects_early"
msgid "Cut dead connects early"
msgstr "Couper tôt les connexions mortes"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Cut dead connects early' setting.
msgctxt "dev_cut_dead_connects_early_detail"
msgid "Drop an exit that has established nothing sooner when two sibling exits are receiving, in ms. Off waits the full 30s connect bar"
msgstr "Écarte plus tôt une sortie qui n’a rien établi quand deux sorties sœurs reçoivent, en ms. Désactivé attend le seuil de connexion complet de 30 s"

#. Developer page: report line when the SDK refused an exit action.
msgctxt "dev_declined_exit"
msgid "No change: the SDK declined that exit"
msgstr "Aucun changement : le SDK a refusé cette sortie"

#. Developer page: heading of the destinations table.
msgctxt "dev_destinations"
msgid "Destinations"
msgstr "Destinations"

#. Developer page: explanation under the destinations table.
msgctxt "dev_destinations_detail"
msgid "Which exit each destination's flows are landing on. A site spread over several rows is a site that lost its single egress IP."
msgstr "Sur quelle sortie arrivent les flux de chaque destination. Un site réparti sur plusieurs lignes est un site qui a perdu son unique IP de sortie."

#. Developer page: page title.
msgctxt "dev_developer"
msgid "Developer"
msgstr "Développeur"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): dial failure rerace control label.
msgctxt "dev_dial_failure_rerace"
msgid "Retry refused connects elsewhere"
msgstr "Réessayer ailleurs les connexions refusées"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'dial failure rerace' control.
msgctxt "dev_dial_failure_rerace_detail"
msgid "When a provider can't reach a site, move the connection to another exit instead of letting it hang"
msgstr "Quand un fournisseur ne peut pas joindre un site, déplace la connexion vers une autre sortie au lieu de la laisser en suspens"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): dial failures control label.
msgctxt "dev_dial_failures"
msgid "Provider connect failures"
msgstr "Échecs de connexion des fournisseurs"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'dial failures' control.
msgctxt "dev_dial_failures_detail"
msgid "Times a provider reported it could not open the upstream connection"
msgstr "Nombre de fois où un fournisseur a signalé ne pas pouvoir ouvrir la connexion amont"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): drop exit control label.
msgctxt "dev_drop_exit"
msgid "Drop"
msgstr "Écarter"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Drop stalled exits fast' setting.
msgctxt "dev_drop_stalled_exits_fast"
msgid "Drop stalled exits fast"
msgstr "Écarter vite les sorties figées"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Drop stalled exits fast' setting.
msgctxt "dev_drop_stalled_exits_fast_detail"
msgid "How long an exit may stop delivering before it is dropped, in ms. Off waits 30s"
msgstr "Combien de temps une sortie peut cesser de livrer avant d’être écartée, en ms. Désactivé attend 30 s"

#. Developer page: report line after an exit was dropped.
msgctxt "dev_dropped_exit"
msgid "Dropped exit"
msgstr "Sortie écartée"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): effective tier control label.
msgctxt "dev_effective_tier"
msgid "Live tier demotion"
msgstr "Rétrogradation de niveau en direct"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'effective tier' control.
msgctxt "dev_effective_tier_detail"
msgid "Failing dials and survived verdicts push a provider down the ranking within a second; promotion back needs clean minutes and a proven connect"
msgstr "Les échecs de connexion et les verdicts survécus font descendre un fournisseur dans le classement en moins d’une seconde ; remonter exige des minutes sans erreur et une connexion prouvée"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): evaluation pool control label.
msgctxt "dev_evaluation_pool"
msgid "Candidates evaluated per slot"
msgstr "Candidats évalués par emplacement"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'evaluation pool' control.
msgctxt "dev_evaluation_pool_detail"
msgid "How many providers a window expansion pings and ranks per slot it needs, keeping the best. 1 evaluates exactly what it needs"
msgstr "Combien de fournisseurs une extension de fenêtre teste par ping et classe pour chaque emplacement nécessaire, en gardant les meilleurs. 1 évalue exactement ce qu’il faut"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): exit dial failures control label.
msgctxt "dev_exit_dial_failures"
msgid "{} failed dials"
msgstr "Connexions échouées : {}"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): exit flows control label.
msgctxt "dev_exit_flows"
msgid "{} flows"
msgstr "Flux : {}"

#. Developer page exit readout: the security policy (safety rules) generation the exit's provider enforces. Connect raises this number with every reviewed change to the built-in rules, so a higher number is newer rules.
msgctxt "dev_exit_policy_generation"
msgid "policy generation {}"
msgstr "génération de politique {}"

#. Developer page exit readout: the exit's provider reported its security policy (safety rules) without a generation, because it predates the generation or runs a custom policy.
msgctxt "dev_exit_policy_generation_unknown"
msgid "policy generation unknown"
msgstr "génération de politique inconnue"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): exits control label.
msgctxt "dev_exits"
msgid "Exits"
msgstr "Sorties"

#. Developer page: explanation of the drop, stall and shuffle actions.
msgctxt "dev_exits_actions_detail"
msgid "Drop, Stall and Shuffle degrade the live connection on purpose, immediately. Nothing here is queued or retried — an action that misses is reported, not replayed."
msgstr "Écarter, Figer et Mélanger dégradent la connexion en cours, volontairement et immédiatement. Rien n’est mis en file d’attente ni relancé ici : une action qui échoue est signalée, pas rejouée."

#. Developer tools screen: action for exporting all diagnostic logs without redaction.
msgctxt "dev_export_all_logs"
msgid "Export all logs (raw)"
msgstr "Exporter tous les journaux (bruts)"

#. Developer tools screen: error shown when diagnostic log export fails.
msgctxt "dev_export_failed"
msgid "Export failed: {}"
msgstr "Échec de l’export : {}"

#. Developer tools screen: explanation that a requested diagnostic item was omitted from an export.
msgctxt "dev_export_not_included"
msgid "Not included: {}"
msgstr "Non inclus : {}"

#. Developer tools screen: action for exporting diagnostic logs with sensitive traffic details redacted.
msgctxt "dev_export_redacted_logs"
msgid "Export redacted logs"
msgstr "Exporter les journaux expurgés"

#. Developer tools screen: action for exporting the selected diagnostic log files.
msgctxt "dev_export_selected"
msgid "Export selected"
msgstr "Exporter la sélection"

#. Developer tools screen: action for sharing a diagnostic bundle.
msgctxt "dev_export_share"
msgid "Share diagnostic bundle"
msgstr "Partager le paquet de diagnostic"

#. Developer tools screen: summary of the number and total size of diagnostic log files exported.
msgctxt "dev_export_summary"
msgid "Exported {0} log file ({1})"
msgid_plural "Exported {0} log files ({1})"
msgstr[0] "{0} fichier journal exporté ({1})"
msgstr[1] "{0} fichiers journaux exportés ({1})"

#. Developer tools screen: explanation that a diagnostic export option is unavailable.
msgctxt "dev_export_unavailable"
msgid "Not available: {}"
msgstr "Indisponible : {}"

#. Developer tools screen: progress label shown while a diagnostic bundle is being exported.
msgctxt "dev_exporting"
msgid "Exporting…"
msgstr "Export en cours…"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Fast first-exit poll' setting.
msgctxt "dev_fast_first_exit_poll"
msgid "Fast first-exit poll"
msgstr "Sondage rapide de la première sortie"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Fast first-exit poll' setting.
msgctxt "dev_fast_first_exit_poll_detail"
msgid "How often a connecting flow re-checks an empty window, in ms, so the first request leaves right after the first exit lands. Off waits the 2s retry pace"
msgstr "Fréquence à laquelle un flux en cours de connexion revérifie une fenêtre vide, en ms, pour que la première requête parte dès que la première sortie arrive. Désactivé attend le rythme de nouvelle tentative de 2 s"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): flows opened control label.
msgctxt "dev_flows_opened"
msgid "Flows opened"
msgstr "Flux ouverts"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'flows opened' control.
msgctxt "dev_flows_opened_detail"
msgid "Total since reset, so runs of different lengths compare"
msgstr "Total depuis la réinitialisation, pour comparer des sessions de durées différentes"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): flows rebound control label.
msgctxt "dev_flows_rebound"
msgid "QUIC flows rebound"
msgstr "Flux QUIC réassociés"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'flows rebound' control.
msgctxt "dev_flows_rebound_detail"
msgid "Flows moved to a warm exit inside a removal; accepted means the server took the path change without a re-dial"
msgstr "Flux déplacés vers une sortie active pendant un retrait ; « accepté » signifie que le serveur a accepté le changement de chemin sans nouvelle connexion"

#. Developer tools screen: formatted value readout for 'flows rebound'.
msgctxt "dev_flows_rebound_value"
msgid "{0} ({1} accepted / {2} re-dialed)"
msgstr "{0} ({1} acceptés / {2} reconnectés)"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): flows reraced control label.
msgctxt "dev_flows_reraced"
msgid "Moved to another exit"
msgstr "Déplacés vers une autre sortie"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'flows reraced' control.
msgctxt "dev_flows_reraced_detail"
msgid "How many of those failures were quietly moved instead of hanging"
msgstr "Combien de ces échecs ont été déplacés discrètement au lieu de rester en suspens"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Follow benched exits' setting.
msgctxt "dev_follow_benched_exits"
msgid "Follow benched exits"
msgstr "Suivre les sorties mises sur la touche"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Follow benched exits' setting.
msgctxt "dev_follow_benched_exits_detail"
msgid "A quarantined exit keeps its own sites' new connections through the early bench, when the verdict is least proven. New sites still avoid it"
msgstr "Une sortie en quarantaine garde les nouvelles connexions de ses propres sites au début de la mise sur la touche, quand le verdict est le moins établi. Les nouveaux sites l’évitent toujours"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Follow window' setting.
msgctxt "dev_follow_window"
msgid "Follow window"
msgstr "Fenêtre de suivi"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Follow window' setting.
msgctxt "dev_follow_window_detail"
msgid "How long into a bench a site's new connections keep following their exit, in ms. Off scatters immediately"
msgstr "Combien de temps après une mise sur la touche les nouvelles connexions d’un site suivent encore leur sortie, en ms. Désactivé disperse immédiatement"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): formation poll control label.
msgctxt "dev_formation_poll"
msgid "Fast first-exit poll"
msgstr "Sondage rapide de la première sortie"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'formation poll' control.
msgctxt "dev_formation_poll_detail"
msgid "How often a connecting flow re-checks an empty window, so the first request leaves right after the first exit lands. Off waits the 2s retry pace"
msgstr "Fréquence à laquelle un flux en cours de connexion revérifie une fenêtre vide, pour que la première requête parte dès que la première sortie arrive. Désactivé attend le rythme de nouvelle tentative de 2 s"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): group follow control label.
msgctxt "dev_group_follow"
msgid "Follow benched exits"
msgstr "Suivre les sorties mises sur la touche"

#. Developer tools: both legacy group-follow controls are not ordinary fresh-flow health overrides.
msgctxt "dev_group_follow_compat_detail"
msgid "Legacy compatibility setting, not a health override. Ordinary new connections never reuse warned or unhealthy exits; they always enter a fresh provider race. Existing connections and explicit pins are unchanged."
msgstr "Ancien réglage de compatibilité, sans dérogation au contrôle de santé. Les nouvelles connexions ordinaires ne réutilisent jamais une sortie avertie ou défaillante ; elles lancent toujours une nouvelle course de fournisseurs. Les connexions existantes et les épinglages explicites ne changent pas."

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'group follow' control.
msgctxt "dev_group_follow_detail"
msgid "A quarantined exit keeps its own sites' new connections through the early bench, when the verdict is least proven, so a bench does not split the site's egress IP. New sites still avoid it. Off scatters them"
msgstr "Une sortie en quarantaine garde les nouvelles connexions de ses propres sites au début de la mise sur la touche, quand le verdict est le moins établi, pour que la mise sur la touche ne divise pas l’IP de sortie du site. Les nouveaux sites l’évitent toujours. Désactivé les disperse"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): group follow window control label.
msgctxt "dev_group_follow_window"
msgid "Follow window"
msgstr "Fenêtre de suivi"

#. Developer page (Apple): the explanation under the 'Follow window' setting, with its unit.
msgctxt "dev_group_follow_window_ms_detail"
msgid "How long into a bench a site's new connections keep following their exit, in ms — early benches are usually false alarms; one that lasts is trending toward removal and stops collecting flows. Off scatters immediately"
msgstr "Combien de temps après une mise sur la touche les nouvelles connexions d’un site suivent encore leur sortie, en ms — les mises sur la touche précoces sont souvent de fausses alertes ; une qui dure tend vers le retrait et cesse de recevoir des flux. Désactivé disperse immédiatement"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): heartbeat control label.
msgctxt "dev_heartbeat"
msgid "State heartbeat"
msgstr "Pouls d’état"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'heartbeat' control.
msgctxt "dev_heartbeat_detail"
msgid "How often one line summarizing live state is written to the log for later forensics. Off silences it; shorter spots a transition, longer keeps more buffer"
msgstr "Fréquence à laquelle une ligne résumant l’état en direct est écrite dans le journal pour une analyse ultérieure. Désactivé la coupe ; plus court repère une transition, plus long garde plus de tampon"

#. Developer page (Apple): the explanation under the 'State heartbeat' setting, with its unit.
msgctxt "dev_heartbeat_ms_detail"
msgid "How often one line summarizing live state is written to the log for later forensics, in ms. Off silences it; shorter spots a transition, longer keeps more buffer"
msgstr "Fréquence à laquelle une ligne résumant l’état en direct est écrite dans le journal pour une analyse ultérieure, en ms. Désactivé la coupe ; plus court repère une transition, plus long garde plus de tampon"

#. Developer page: intro line under the title.
msgctxt "dev_intro"
msgid "Tools for diagnosing connection freezes. These act on the live connection."
msgstr "Outils pour diagnostiquer les blocages de connexion. Ils agissent sur la connexion en cours."

#. Developer screen: title of the control-plane IP family setting.
msgctxt "dev_ip_family"
msgid "Control connections"
msgstr "Connexions de contrôle"

#. Developer screen: the automatic IP family option.
msgctxt "dev_ip_family_auto"
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr "Automatique"

#. Developer screen: the automatic option's detail when one family was demoted; {reason} is the demotion reason.
msgctxt "dev_ip_family_auto_demoted_detail"
msgid "Automatic. {}."
msgstr "Automatique. {}."

#. Developer screen: detail line of the automatic IP family option.
msgctxt "dev_ip_family_auto_detail"
msgid "Uses whichever family connects first, and routes around one that fails after connecting."
msgstr "Utilise la famille qui se connecte en premier et contourne celle qui échoue après la connexion."

#. Developer screen: the IPv4-only option.
msgctxt "dev_ip_family_force4"
msgid "Force IPv4"
msgstr "Forcer IPv4"

#. Developer screen: detail line of the IPv4-only option.
msgctxt "dev_ip_family_force4_detail"
msgid "Control-plane connections use IPv4 only. Turn this off on an IPv6-only network."
msgstr "Les connexions de contrôle n’utilisent qu’IPv4. Désactivez cette option sur un réseau uniquement IPv6."

#. Developer screen: the IPv6-only option.
msgctxt "dev_ip_family_force6"
msgid "Force IPv6"
msgstr "Forcer IPv6"

#. Developer screen: detail line of the IPv6-only option.
msgctxt "dev_ip_family_force6_detail"
msgid "Control-plane connections use IPv6 only. Turn this off if the app cannot reach the server."
msgstr "Les connexions de contrôle n’utilisent qu’IPv6. Désactivez cette option si l’application ne joint pas le serveur."

#. Developer page: label of the 'Keep quiet providers longer' setting.
msgctxt "dev_keep_quiet_providers_longer"
msgid "Keep quiet providers longer"
msgstr "Garder plus longtemps les fournisseurs silencieux"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Keep quiet providers longer' setting.
msgctxt "dev_keep_quiet_providers_longer_detail"
msgid "How long a provider still acknowledging traffic may return nothing before it is dropped, in ms. Off keeps them until they stop acknowledging"
msgstr "Combien de temps un fournisseur qui acquitte encore le trafic peut ne rien renvoyer avant d’être écarté, en ms. Désactivé les garde jusqu’à ce qu’ils cessent d’acquitter"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): load corroboration control label.
msgctxt "dev_load_corroboration"
msgid "Load corroboration"
msgstr "Corroboration par la charge"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'load corroboration' control.
msgctxt "dev_load_corroboration_detail"
msgid "Extra silent destinations required per this many flows before a busy exit can be benched on soft evidence: a 24-flow exit at 8 needs 3 silent sites, not 2. Off keeps the flat minimum"
msgstr "Destinations silencieuses supplémentaires exigées par tranche de ce nombre de flux avant qu’une sortie chargée puisse être mise sur la touche sur des indices faibles : une sortie de 24 flux à 8 exige 3 sites silencieux, pas 2. Désactivé garde le minimum fixe"

#. Developer tools screen: control label for diagnostic log detail.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity"
msgid "Log detail"
msgstr "Détail des journaux"

#. Developer tools screen: default diagnostic log detail level.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_default"
msgid "Default"
msgstr "Par défaut"

#. Developer tools screen: explanation of the default diagnostic log detail level.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_default_detail"
msgid "Connection errors and contract pings"
msgstr "Erreurs de connexion et pings de contrat"

#. Developer tools screen: trace diagnostic log detail level.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_trace"
msgid "Trace"
msgstr "Trace"

#. Developer tools screen: explanation of the trace diagnostic log detail level.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_trace_detail"
msgid "Transport and window internals. Very large logs"
msgstr "Fonctionnement interne du transport et de la fenêtre. Journaux très volumineux"

#. Developer tools screen: label used when the diagnostic log detail level cannot be read.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_unavailable"
msgid "Unavailable"
msgstr "Indisponible"

#. Developer tools screen: explanation shown when the diagnostic log detail level cannot be read.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_unavailable_detail"
msgid "There is no device to read the log level from yet. Sign in first"
msgstr "Il n’y a pas encore d’appareil sur lequel lire le niveau de journal. Connectez-vous d’abord"

#. Developer tools screen: verbose diagnostic log detail level.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_verbose"
msgid "Verbose"
msgstr "Détaillé"

#. Developer tools screen: explanation of the verbose diagnostic log detail level.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_verbose_detail"
msgid "Contract accounting and per-packet block decisions. Includes destination IP addresses"
msgstr "Comptabilité des contrats et décisions de blocage par paquet. Inclut les adresses IP de destination"

#. Developer tools screen: privacy warning shown when detailed traffic logging is enabled.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_warning"
msgid "At Verbose and above the logs contain the destination IP addresses and ports of the traffic you send. Use “Export redacted logs” to share them; the raw bundle should not leave this device."
msgstr "À partir de « Détaillé », les journaux contiennent les adresses IP et les ports de destination du trafic que vous envoyez. Utilisez « Exporter les journaux expurgés » pour les partager ; le paquet brut ne doit pas quitter cet appareil."

#. Developer tools screen: title for the detailed traffic logging privacy warning.
msgctxt "dev_log_verbosity_warning_title"
msgid "Logs are recording your real traffic"
msgstr "Les journaux enregistrent votre trafic réel"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Longer TCP idle timeout' setting.
msgctxt "dev_longer_tcp_idle_timeout"
msgid "Longer TCP idle timeout"
msgstr "Délai d’inactivité TCP plus long"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Longer TCP idle timeout' setting.
msgctxt "dev_longer_tcp_idle_timeout_detail"
msgid "How long a TCP connection may sit idle, in ms. Off uses the UDP bound"
msgstr "Combien de temps une connexion TCP peut rester inactive, en ms. Désactivé utilise la limite UDP"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): max flows per exit control label.
msgctxt "dev_max_flows_per_exit"
msgid "Max connections per exit"
msgstr "Connexions max par sortie"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'max flows per exit' control.
msgctxt "dev_max_flows_per_exit_detail"
msgid "Losing an exit kills every connection on it. Lower spreads the damage; a site may then use more than one exit IP"
msgstr "Perdre une sortie coupe toutes ses connexions. Plus bas répartit les dégâts ; un site peut alors utiliser plusieurs IP de sortie"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): measure none control label.
msgctxt "dev_measure_none"
msgid "No provider failures yet. Stall an exit below to cause one."
msgstr "Aucune panne de fournisseur pour l’instant. Figez une sortie ci-dessous pour en provoquer une."

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): measurements control label.
msgctxt "dev_measurements"
msgid "Measurements"
msgstr "Mesures"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'measurements' control.
msgctxt "dev_measurements_detail"
msgid "What a provider failure costs. Reset, run a test, read back."
msgstr "Ce que coûte une panne de fournisseur. Réinitialisez, lancez un test, relisez."

#. Developer page: button that migrates the live connection.
msgctxt "dev_migrate"
msgid "Migrate"
msgstr "Migrer"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): migrate exit control label.
msgctxt "dev_migrate_exit"
msgid "Migrate"
msgstr "Migrer"

#. Developer page: last-action report after moving an exit's flows to another exit; the exit's short id follows.
msgctxt "dev_migrated_exit"
msgid "Migrated exit"
msgstr "Sortie migrée"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): min blackhole destinations control label.
msgctxt "dev_min_blackhole_destinations"
msgid "Corroborate silent exits"
msgstr "Corroborer les sorties silencieuses"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'min blackhole destinations' control.
msgctxt "dev_min_blackhole_destinations_detail"
msgid "How many distinct destinations must be silent before an exit is convicted on no-receive, so one dead site cannot remove a working exit. Off lets a single destination convict"
msgstr "Combien de destinations distinctes doivent rester silencieuses avant qu’une sortie soit condamnée pour absence de réception, pour qu’un seul site en panne ne puisse pas retirer une sortie qui fonctionne. Désactivé laisse une seule destination condamner"

#. Developer page: value of the flows that never came back, {done} of {total}.
msgctxt "dev_never_came_back_value"
msgid "{0} of {1}"
msgstr "{0} sur {1}"

#. Developer page: empty state of the destinations table.
msgctxt "dev_no_destinations"
msgid "No destinations yet."
msgstr "Aucune destination pour l’instant."

#. Developer page: shown when there is no session to act on.
msgctxt "dev_no_device"
msgid "No session. Sign in and connect to use these tools."
msgstr "Aucune session. Connectez-vous à votre compte et au réseau pour utiliser ces outils."

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): no exits control label.
msgctxt "dev_no_exits"
msgid "No exits. Connect first."
msgstr "Aucune sortie. Connectez-vous d’abord."

#. Developer page: empty state of the probe results table.
msgctxt "dev_no_probe_results"
msgid "No probe results yet. Start the suite."
msgstr "Aucun résultat de sondage pour l’instant. Lancez la série."

#. Developer page: empty state of the provider failures table.
msgctxt "dev_no_provider_failures"
msgid "No provider failures yet."
msgstr "Aucune défaillance de fournisseur pour l’instant."

#. Developer page: report line when no reliability override is in force.
msgctxt "dev_not_applied"
msgid "Not applied: there is no reliability override in force to change."
msgstr "Non appliqué : aucun remplacement de fiabilité n’est en vigueur à modifier."

#. Developer page: report line when there is no live session to act on.
msgctxt "dev_not_issued"
msgid "Not issued: there is no live session to act on."
msgstr "Non envoyé : aucune session en cours sur laquelle agir."

#. Developer page: note shown when no reliability override is in force.
msgctxt "dev_nothing_in_force"
msgid "No reliability override is in force, so the settings sections are hidden rather than shown at zero. The measurements and exit readout below are live."
msgstr "Aucun remplacement de fiabilité n’est en vigueur : les sections de réglages sont donc masquées plutôt qu’affichées à zéro. Les mesures et l’état des sorties ci-dessous sont en direct."

#. Developer page: what a setting's 0 means when it falls back to the minimum of 1 ('Candidates evaluated per slot').
msgctxt "dev_one_min"
msgid "1 (min)"
msgstr "1 (min.)"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): open tools control label.
msgctxt "dev_open_tools"
msgid "Open developer tools"
msgstr "Ouvrir les outils de développement"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): probe all control label.
msgctxt "dev_probe_all"
msgid "Probe all exits now"
msgstr "Sonder toutes les sorties maintenant"

#. Developer page: button that probes every exit now.
msgctxt "dev_probe_all_exits_now"
msgid "Probe all exits now"
msgstr "Sonder toutes les sorties maintenant"

#. Developer page: probe outcome, failed.
msgctxt "dev_probe_failed"
msgid "failed"
msgstr "échec"

#. Developer page: probe outcome, ok.
msgctxt "dev_probe_ok"
msgid "ok"
msgstr "ok"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): probe providers control label.
msgctxt "dev_probe_providers"
msgid "Probe providers"
msgstr "Sonder les fournisseurs"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'probe providers' control.
msgctxt "dev_probe_providers_detail"
msgid "Qualify exits by dialing real sites through them. An answer proves the exit; silence never counts against it"
msgstr "Qualifie les sorties en joignant de vrais sites à travers elles. Une réponse prouve la sortie ; le silence ne compte jamais contre elle"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): probe sample hosts control label.
msgctxt "dev_probe_sample_hosts"
msgid "Probe hosts per pass"
msgstr "Hôtes sondés par passe"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'probe sample hosts' control.
msgctxt "dev_probe_sample_hosts_detail"
msgid "How many health sites one qualification pass dials through an exit. 0 probes the entire embedded list; a smaller number rotates through it in blocks"
msgstr "Combien de sites de contrôle une passe de qualification joint à travers une sortie. 0 sonde toute la liste intégrée ; un nombre plus petit la parcourt par blocs"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Probe silence streak' setting.
msgctxt "dev_probe_silence_streak"
msgid "Probe silence streak"
msgstr "Série de sondages silencieux"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Probe silence streak' setting.
msgctxt "dev_probe_silence_streak_detail"
msgid "How many consecutive probe passes an exit may answer with total silence before it is warned out of new-flow placement. Placement only"
msgstr "Combien de passes de sondage consécutives une sortie peut laisser sans aucune réponse avant d’être avertie et exclue du placement des nouveaux flux. Placement uniquement"

#. Developer page (Apple): the explanation under the 'Probe silence streak' setting.
msgctxt "dev_probe_silence_streak_long_detail"
msgid "How many consecutive probe passes an exit may answer with total silence before it is warned out of new-flow placement — the compensation for providers that leave the network mid-session. Placement only: removal stays traffic-based, and any sign of life clears the streak"
msgstr "Combien de passes de sondage consécutives une sortie peut laisser sans aucune réponse avant d’être avertie et exclue du placement des nouveaux flux — la compensation pour les fournisseurs qui quittent le réseau en cours de session. Placement uniquement : le retrait reste fondé sur le trafic, et le moindre signe de vie remet la série à zéro"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Probe stalled exits before dropping' setting.
msgctxt "dev_probe_stalled_exits"
msgid "Probe stalled exits before dropping"
msgstr "Sonder les sorties figées avant de les écarter"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Probe stalled exits before dropping' setting.
msgctxt "dev_probe_stalled_exits_detail"
msgid "When an exit stalls, ping it once before convicting. A congested but alive exit answers and keeps its flows; a dead one is still dropped"
msgstr "Quand une sortie se fige, elle reçoit un ping avant d’être condamnée. Une sortie congestionnée mais vivante répond et garde ses flux ; une sortie morte est quand même écartée"

#. Developer page: heading of the probe suite section.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite"
msgid "Probe suite"
msgstr "Série de sondages"

#. Developer page: explanation of the probe suite.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite_detail"
msgid "Dials real targets through the live connection and times each stage. Runs with the SDK's own default configuration."
msgstr "Contacte de vraies cibles via la connexion en cours et chronomètre chaque étape. S’exécute avec la configuration par défaut du SDK lui-même."

#. Developer page: probe suite status when it is not running.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite_idle"
msgid "Not running."
msgstr "À l’arrêt."

#. Developer page: report line when the probe suite could not start.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite_not_started"
msgid "Probe suite did not start: no live session, or one is already running."
msgstr "La série de sondages n’a pas démarré : aucune session en cours, ou une série est déjà en cours."

#. Developer page: probe suite status while it runs.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite_running"
msgid "Running."
msgstr "En cours."

#. Developer page: button that starts the probe suite.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite_start"
msgid "Start probe suite"
msgstr "Lancer la série de sondages"

#. Developer page: report line after the probe suite started.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite_started"
msgid "Probe suite started"
msgstr "Série de sondages lancée"

#. Developer page: button that stops the probe suite.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite_stop"
msgid "Stop"
msgstr "Arrêter"

#. Developer page: report line after the probe suite stopped.
msgctxt "dev_probe_suite_stopped"
msgid "Probe suite stopped"
msgstr "Série de sondages arrêtée"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): probe timeout control label.
msgctxt "dev_probe_timeout"
msgid "Probe wait"
msgstr "Attente de la sonde"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'probe timeout' control.
msgctxt "dev_probe_timeout_detail"
msgid "How long a qualification probe waits for an answer. Off uses the built-in 4s. It only bounds waiting for proof, it never convicts"
msgstr "Combien de temps une sonde de qualification attend une réponse. Désactivé utilise les 4 s intégrées. Elle borne seulement l’attente d’une preuve, elle ne condamne jamais"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Probe wait' setting.
msgctxt "dev_probe_wait"
msgid "Probe wait"
msgstr "Attente de la sonde"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Probe wait' setting.
msgctxt "dev_probe_wait_detail"
msgid "How long a qualification probe waits for an answer, in ms. Off uses the built-in 4s. It only bounds waiting for proof, it never convicts"
msgstr "Combien de temps une sonde de qualification attend une réponse, en ms. Désactivé utilise les 4 s intégrées. Elle borne seulement l’attente d’une preuve, elle ne condamne jamais"

#. Developer page: heading of the probed exits table.
msgctxt "dev_probed_exits"
msgid "Probed exits"
msgstr "Sorties sondées"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): probes control label.
msgctxt "dev_probes"
msgid "Probes"
msgstr "Sondes"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'probes' control.
msgctxt "dev_probes_detail"
msgid "Qualification probes this session"
msgstr "Sondes de qualification de cette session"

#. Developer tools screen: formatted value readout for 'probes'.
msgctxt "dev_probes_value"
msgid "{0} sent / {1} answered"
msgstr "{0} envoyées / {1} répondues"

#. Developer page: value of the QUIC flows that rebound: {count} total, {accepted} accepted, {redialed} re-dialed.
msgctxt "dev_quic_flows_rebound_value"
msgid "{0} ({1} accepted / {2} re-dialed)"
msgstr "{0} ({1} acceptés / {2} reconnectés)"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): quic rebind control label.
msgctxt "dev_quic_rebind"
msgid "Rebind QUIC on exit loss"
msgstr "Réassocier QUIC à la perte d’une sortie"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'quic rebind' control.
msgctxt "dev_quic_rebind_detail"
msgid "Re-pin established QUIC flows to a live exit inside the removal instead of tearing them down"
msgstr "Réépingle les flux QUIC établis sur une sortie active pendant le retrait au lieu de les couper"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): recovery control label.
msgctxt "dev_recovery"
msgid "Recovery time"
msgstr "Temps de rétablissement"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'recovery' control.
msgctxt "dev_recovery_detail"
msgid "From an exit dying to that site answering again"
msgstr "De la mort d’une sortie jusqu’à ce que ce site réponde à nouveau"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): recovery missed control label.
msgctxt "dev_recovery_missed"
msgid "Never came back"
msgstr "Jamais revenus"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'recovery missed' control.
msgctxt "dev_recovery_missed_detail"
msgid "Sites abandoned rather than recovered"
msgstr "Sites abandonnés plutôt que rétablis"

#. Developer tools screen: formatted value readout for 'recovery missed'.
msgctxt "dev_recovery_missed_value"
msgid "{0} of {1}"
msgstr "{0} sur {1}"

#. Developer page: value of the recovery time, {average} and {worst} are durations.
msgctxt "dev_recovery_time_value"
msgid "avg {0}, worst {1}"
msgstr "moy. {0}, pire {1}"

#. Developer tools screen: formatted value readout for 'recovery'.
msgctxt "dev_recovery_value"
msgid "avg {0}, worst {1}"
msgstr "moy. {0}, pire {1}"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): refresh control label.
msgctxt "dev_refresh"
msgid "Refresh"
msgstr "Actualiser"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Release stuck retransmits' setting.
msgctxt "dev_release_stuck_retransmits"
msgid "Release stuck retransmits"
msgstr "Libérer les retransmissions bloquées"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Release stuck retransmits' setting.
msgctxt "dev_release_stuck_retransmits_detail"
msgid "How long retransmits are held before one is released, in ms. Off waits 30s"
msgstr "Combien de temps les retransmissions sont retenues avant d’en libérer une, en ms. Désactivé attend 30 s"

#. Windows Developer page: the title of the second pane, which holds the reliability overrides, and its name for screen readers.
msgctxt "dev_reliability_overrides"
msgid "Reliability overrides"
msgstr "Remplacements de fiabilité"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): removal budget count control label.
msgctxt "dev_removal_budget_count"
msgid "Removal storm limit"
msgstr "Limite de tempête de retraits"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'removal budget count' control.
msgctxt "dev_removal_budget_count_detail"
msgid "How many verdict removals are allowed per window before the rest are deferred; a burst is more likely one local cause than many failures. Off removes without limit"
msgstr "Combien de retraits sur verdict sont permis par fenêtre avant que les suivants soient différés ; une rafale vient plus probablement d’une cause locale que de nombreuses pannes. Désactivé retire sans limite"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): removal budget window control label.
msgctxt "dev_removal_budget_window"
msgid "Removal storm window"
msgstr "Fenêtre de tempête de retraits"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'removal budget window' control.
msgctxt "dev_removal_budget_window_detail"
msgid "The window the removal limit is counted over. Off (like a limit of 0) turns the breaker off"
msgstr "La fenêtre sur laquelle la limite de retraits est comptée. Désactivé (comme une limite de 0) coupe le disjoncteur"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Removal storm limit' setting.
msgctxt "dev_removal_storm_limit"
msgid "Removal storm limit"
msgstr "Limite de tempête de retraits"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Removal storm limit' setting.
msgctxt "dev_removal_storm_limit_detail"
msgid "How many verdict removals are allowed per window before the rest are deferred; a burst is more likely one local cause than many failures"
msgstr "Combien de retraits sur verdict sont permis par fenêtre avant que les suivants soient différés ; une rafale vient plus probablement d’une cause locale que de nombreuses pannes"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Removal storm window' setting.
msgctxt "dev_removal_storm_window"
msgid "Removal storm window"
msgstr "Fenêtre de tempête de retraits"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Removal storm window' setting.
msgctxt "dev_removal_storm_window_detail"
msgid "The window the removal limit is counted over, in ms. Off (like a limit of 0) turns the breaker off"
msgstr "La fenêtre sur laquelle la limite de retraits est comptée, en ms. Désactivé (comme une limite de 0) coupe le disjoncteur"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): removals deferred control label.
msgctxt "dev_removals_deferred"
msgid "Removals deferred"
msgstr "Retraits différés"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'removals deferred' control.
msgctxt "dev_removals_deferred_detail"
msgid "Removals the storm breaker held back after a correlated burst"
msgstr "Retraits que le disjoncteur de tempête a retenus après une rafale corrélée"

#. Developer page: label before the requested value of an override.
msgctxt "dev_requested"
msgid "Requested:"
msgstr "Demandé :"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): reset defaults control label.
msgctxt "dev_reset_defaults"
msgid "Reset to shipped defaults"
msgstr "Rétablir les valeurs d’origine"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): reset measurements control label.
msgctxt "dev_reset_measurements"
msgid "Reset measurements"
msgstr "Réinitialiser les mesures"

#. Developer page: button that resets the reliability settings.
msgctxt "dev_reset_to_shipped_defaults"
msgid "Reset to shipped defaults"
msgstr "Rétablir les valeurs d’origine"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): scheduler pause recovery control label.
msgctxt "dev_scheduler_pause_recovery"
msgid "Suspend recovery window"
msgstr "Fenêtre de reprise après veille"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'scheduler pause recovery' control.
msgctxt "dev_scheduler_pause_recovery_detail"
msgid "How long verdicts stay held after a detected suspend, giving transports time to re-register. Off uses the built-in 5s"
msgstr "Combien de temps les verdicts restent retenus après une mise en veille détectée, le temps que les transports se réenregistrent. Désactivé utilise les 5 s intégrées"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): scheduler pause tolerance control label.
msgctxt "dev_scheduler_pause_tolerance"
msgid "Suspend detector"
msgstr "Détecteur de veille"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'scheduler pause tolerance' control.
msgctxt "dev_scheduler_pause_tolerance_detail"
msgid "How much timer overshoot reads as the phone being suspended rather than an exit stalling, so a resumed phone does not convict every exit at once. Off disables it"
msgstr "Quel dépassement de minuterie est interprété comme une mise en veille du téléphone plutôt que comme une sortie figée, pour qu’un téléphone qui se réveille ne condamne pas toutes les sorties d’un coup. Désactivé le coupe"

#. Developer page (Apple): the explanation under the 'Suspend detector' setting, with its unit.
msgctxt "dev_scheduler_pause_tolerance_ms_detail"
msgid "How much timer overshoot reads as the phone being suspended rather than an exit stalling, in ms, so a resumed phone does not convict every exit at once. Off disables it"
msgstr "Quel dépassement de minuterie est interprété comme une mise en veille du téléphone plutôt que comme une sortie figée, en ms, pour qu’un téléphone qui se réveille ne condamne pas toutes les sorties d’un coup. Désactivé le coupe"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): scheduler pauses control label.
msgctxt "dev_scheduler_pauses"
msgid "Suspends caught"
msgstr "Mises en veille détectées"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'scheduler pauses' control.
msgctxt "dev_scheduler_pauses_detail"
msgid "Host suspends the detector caught, each one a batch of verdicts held instead of executed on a just-resumed phone"
msgstr "Mises en veille de l’hôte repérées par le détecteur, chacune étant un lot de verdicts retenus au lieu d’être exécutés sur un téléphone tout juste réveillé"

#. Developer tools screen: section heading for the detection controls.
msgctxt "dev_section_detection"
msgid "Detection"
msgstr "Détection"

#. Developer tools screen: section heading for diagnostic log controls.
msgctxt "dev_section_diagnostics"
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr "Diagnostic"

#. Developer tools screen: section heading for the observability controls.
msgctxt "dev_section_observability"
msgid "Observability"
msgstr "Observabilité"

#. Developer tools screen: section heading for the placement controls.
msgctxt "dev_section_placement"
msgid "Placement"
msgstr "Placement"

#. Developer tools screen: section heading for the probing controls.
msgctxt "dev_section_probing"
msgid "Probing"
msgstr "Sondage"

#. Developer tools screen: section heading for the recovery controls.
msgctxt "dev_section_recovery"
msgid "Recovery"
msgstr "Rétablissement"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): send stall control label.
msgctxt "dev_send_stall"
msgid "Drop stalled exits fast"
msgstr "Écarter vite les sorties figées"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'send stall' control.
msgctxt "dev_send_stall_detail"
msgid "How long an exit may stop delivering before it is dropped. Off waits 30s"
msgstr "Combien de temps une sortie peut cesser de livrer avant d’être écartée. Désactivé attend 30 s"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): server name bridge control label.
msgctxt "dev_server_name_bridge"
msgid "Converge late-named flows"
msgstr "Faire converger les flux nommés tard"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'server name bridge' control.
msgctxt "dev_server_name_bridge_detail"
msgid "Moves later connections onto the exit the first one already uses"
msgstr "Déplace les connexions suivantes vers la sortie que la première utilise déjà"

#. Developer page: shown when the system service is not attached.
msgctxt "dev_service_detached"
msgid "The URnetwork service is not attached, so the live connection cannot be read."
msgstr "Le service URnetwork n’est pas rattaché : la connexion en cours ne peut donc pas être lue."

#. Developer page: heading of the daemon session log.
msgctxt "dev_session_log"
msgid "Session log"
msgstr "Journal de session"

#. Developer page: shown when this account may not read the daemon log.
msgctxt "dev_session_log_denied"
msgid "This account may drive the daemon but may not read its log."
msgstr "Ce compte peut piloter le service, mais pas lire son journal."

#. Developer page: explanation of the session log.
msgctxt "dev_session_log_detail"
msgid "What the daemon has written since it started. The reliability lines ([rel] event=...) are how a knob below proves it changed something."
msgstr "Ce que le service a écrit depuis son démarrage. Les lignes de fiabilité ([rel] event=...) montrent qu’un réglage ci-dessous a bien changé quelque chose."

#. Developer page: line in the session log when {count} earlier lines were dropped.
msgctxt "dev_session_log_dropped"
msgid "{} lines were dropped before this point"
msgstr "Lignes supprimées avant ce point : {}"

#. Developer page: empty state of the session log.
msgctxt "dev_session_log_empty"
msgid "The daemon has not written anything yet."
msgstr "Le service n’a encore rien écrit."

#. Developer page: toggle that follows the session log tail.
msgctxt "dev_session_log_follow"
msgid "Follow"
msgstr "Suivre"

#. Developer page: note when the daemon restarted and the log began again.
msgctxt "dev_session_log_restarted"
msgid "The daemon restarted. This is a new log; the previous run's lines are gone."
msgstr "Le service a redémarré. Ceci est un nouveau journal ; les lignes de l’exécution précédente ont disparu."

#. Developer page (Apple): button that applies a typed value.
msgctxt "dev_set"
msgid "Set"
msgstr "Appliquer"

#. Developer page (Apple): button that shares an exported log file. {name} is the file name.
msgctxt "dev_share_file"
msgid "Share {}"
msgstr "Partager {}"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): shuffle exits control label.
msgctxt "dev_shuffle_exits"
msgid "Shuffle all exits"
msgstr "Mélanger toutes les sorties"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): simulate network change control label.
msgctxt "dev_simulate_network_change"
msgid "Simulate network change"
msgstr "Simuler un changement de réseau"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): soft verdict control label.
msgctxt "dev_soft_verdict"
msgid "Demote before removing"
msgstr "Rétrograder avant de retirer"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'soft verdict' control.
msgctxt "dev_soft_verdict_detail"
msgid "Ambiguous verdicts bench an exit instead of tearing down its flows; removal needs sustained evidence or an empty exit"
msgstr "Les verdicts ambigus mettent une sortie sur la touche au lieu de couper ses flux ; le retrait exige des indices persistants ou une sortie vide"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): stall exit control label.
msgctxt "dev_stall_exit"
msgid "Stall"
msgstr "Figer"

#. Developer page: report line after an exit was stalled.
msgctxt "dev_stalled_exit"
msgid "Stalled exit"
msgstr "Sortie figée"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): standing reserve control label.
msgctxt "dev_standing_reserve"
msgid "Keep a spare exit warm"
msgstr "Garder une sortie de réserve prête"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'standing reserve' control.
msgctxt "dev_standing_reserve_detail"
msgid "Size each window one exit beyond its target so a replacement is already connected. Off waits until a loss to backfill"
msgstr "Dimensionne chaque fenêtre avec une sortie de plus que sa cible pour qu’un remplaçant soit déjà connecté. Désactivé attend une perte pour compléter"

#. Developer page: exit state, benched.
msgctxt "dev_state_benched"
msgid "benched"
msgstr "sur la touche"

#. Developer page: exit state, done.
msgctxt "dev_state_done"
msgid "done"
msgstr "terminée"

#. Developer page: label of the 'State heartbeat' setting.
msgctxt "dev_state_heartbeat"
msgid "State heartbeat"
msgstr "Pouls d’état"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'State heartbeat' setting.
msgctxt "dev_state_heartbeat_detail"
msgid "How often one line summarizing live state is written to the log for later forensics, in ms. Off silences it"
msgstr "Fréquence à laquelle une ligne résumant l’état en direct est écrite dans le journal pour une analyse ultérieure, en ms. Désactivé la coupe"

#. Developer page: exit state of an exit that carries only the P2P transport. A transport name; never translated.
msgctxt "dev_state_p2p"
msgid "p2p"
msgstr "p2p"

#. Developer page: exit state, proven.
msgctxt "dev_state_proven"
msgid "proven"
msgstr "éprouvée"

#. Developer page exit readout: the exit's tier in its state line, the platform's rank for the provider (0 is best). The value is the tier number, or two numbers with an arrow ("1→3") when live demotion moved the rank that selection uses. The Windows and Linux pages show the same value in their Tier column (dev_col_tier).
msgctxt "dev_state_tier"
msgid "tier {}"
msgstr "niveau {}"

#. Developer page: exit state, warned.
msgctxt "dev_state_warned"
msgid "warned"
msgstr "avertie"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Sticky site affinity' setting.
msgctxt "dev_sticky_site_affinity"
msgid "Sticky site affinity"
msgstr "Affinité persistante par site"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Sticky site affinity' setting.
msgctxt "dev_sticky_site_affinity_detail"
msgid "A site's new connections stay on the exit its earlier ones already use, even past the flow cap, so a busy site keeps one egress IP"
msgstr "Les nouvelles connexions d’un site restent sur la sortie que ses connexions précédentes utilisent déjà, même au-delà du plafond de flux, pour qu’un site chargé garde une seule IP de sortie"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Suspend detector' setting.
msgctxt "dev_suspend_detector"
msgid "Suspend detector"
msgstr "Détecteur de veille"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Suspend detector' setting.
msgctxt "dev_suspend_detector_detail"
msgid "How much timer overshoot reads as the machine being suspended rather than an exit stalling, in ms, so a resumed machine does not convict every exit at once. Off disables it"
msgstr "Quel dépassement de minuterie est interprété comme une mise en veille de l’ordinateur plutôt que comme une sortie figée, en ms, pour qu’un ordinateur qui se réveille ne condamne pas toutes les sorties d’un coup. Désactivé le coupe"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Suspend recovery window' setting.
msgctxt "dev_suspend_recovery_window"
msgid "Suspend recovery window"
msgstr "Fenêtre de reprise après veille"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Suspend recovery window' setting.
msgctxt "dev_suspend_recovery_window_detail"
msgid "How long verdicts stay held after a detected suspend, in ms, giving transports time to re-register. Off uses the built-in 5s"
msgstr "Combien de temps les verdicts restent retenus après une mise en veille détectée, en ms, le temps que les transports se réenregistrent. Désactivé utilise les 5 s intégrées"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Suspends caught' setting.
msgctxt "dev_suspends_caught"
msgid "Suspends caught"
msgstr "Mises en veille détectées"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Suspends caught' setting.
msgctxt "dev_suspends_caught_detail"
msgid "Host suspends the detector caught, each one a batch of verdicts held instead of executed on a just-resumed machine"
msgstr "Mises en veille de l’hôte repérées par le détecteur, chacune étant un lot de verdicts retenus au lieu d’être exécutés sur un ordinateur tout juste réveillé"

#. Developer page: button that syncs the reliability settings.
msgctxt "dev_sync"
msgid "Sync"
msgstr "Synchroniser"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): tcp collapse hold control label.
msgctxt "dev_tcp_collapse_hold"
msgid "Release stuck retransmits"
msgstr "Libérer les retransmissions bloquées"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'tcp collapse hold' control.
msgctxt "dev_tcp_collapse_hold_detail"
msgid "How long retransmits are held before one is released. Off waits 30s"
msgstr "Combien de temps les retransmissions sont retenues avant d’en libérer une. Désactivé attend 30 s"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): tcp idle timeout control label.
msgctxt "dev_tcp_idle_timeout"
msgid "Longer TCP idle timeout"
msgstr "Délai d’inactivité TCP plus long"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'tcp idle timeout' control.
msgctxt "dev_tcp_idle_timeout_detail"
msgid "How long a TCP connection may sit idle. Off uses the UDP bound"
msgstr "Combien de temps une connexion TCP peut rester inactive. Désactivé utilise la limite UDP"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): timing control label.
msgctxt "dev_timing"
msgid "Timing"
msgstr "Délais"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): udp idle timeout control label.
msgctxt "dev_udp_idle_timeout"
msgid "UDP idle timeout"
msgstr "Délai d’inactivité UDP"

#. Developer page: label of the 'UDP idle timeout' setting (desktop wording of dev_udp_idle_timeout).
msgctxt "dev_udp_idle_timeout_desktop"
msgid "UDP idle timeout"
msgstr "Délai d’inactivité UDP"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'UDP idle timeout' setting, with the unit the number box takes.
msgctxt "dev_udp_idle_timeout_desktop_detail"
msgid "How long a non-TCP flow may sit idle before it is reaped, in ms"
msgstr "Combien de temps un flux non TCP peut rester inactif avant d’être fermé, en ms"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'udp idle timeout' control.
msgctxt "dev_udp_idle_timeout_detail"
msgid "How long a non-TCP flow may sit idle before it is reaped"
msgstr "Combien de temps un flux non TCP peut rester inactif avant d’être fermé"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): udp teardown control label.
msgctxt "dev_udp_teardown"
msgid "Signal UDP teardown"
msgstr "Signaler la fermeture UDP"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'udp teardown' control.
msgctxt "dev_udp_teardown_detail"
msgid "Tells DNS and QUIC the path is gone instead of going silent"
msgstr "Indique à DNS et QUIC que le chemin a disparu au lieu de se taire"

#. Developer page: what a setting's 0 means when it removes the cap ('Max connections per exit').
msgctxt "dev_unlimited"
msgid "Unlimited"
msgstr "Illimité"

#. Developer page: per-exit button that releases an exit stalled with Stall.
msgctxt "dev_unstall"
msgid "Unstall"
msgstr "Défiger"

#. Developer page: report line after a stall was cleared on an exit.
msgctxt "dev_unstalled_exit"
msgid "Cleared stall on exit"
msgstr "Sortie défigée"

#. Developer page, and the line under Linux Settings > Check for updates: report line when the update check failed.
msgctxt "dev_update_check_failed"
msgid "The update check failed — see the app log."
msgstr "La recherche de mises à jour a échoué — consultez le journal de l’application."

#. Developer page, and the line under Linux Settings > Check for updates: update check status while checking.
msgctxt "dev_update_checking"
msgid "Checking for updates…"
msgstr "Recherche de mises à jour…"

#. Developer page, and the line under Linux Settings > Check for updates: update check result on a development build. {version} is the newest release version.
msgctxt "dev_update_dev_build"
msgid "Development build: the newest release is v{}, and a development build is never updated automatically."
msgstr "Version de développement : la dernière version publiée est la v{}, et une version de développement n’est jamais mise à jour automatiquement."

#. Developer page (Windows): the rest of the development build line, after the version.
msgctxt "dev_update_dev_build_note"
msgid "this is a dev build (code 0), which never self-updates"
msgstr "c’est une version de développement (code 0), qui ne se met jamais à jour elle-même"

#. Developer page: update check result when a newer release exists; Settings shows the update. {version} is the release version.
msgctxt "dev_update_found"
msgid "Update available: v{} — see Settings."
msgstr "Mise à jour disponible : v{} — voir Paramètres."

#. Developer page (Windows): prefix of the update check result when a newer release exists; the version follows.
msgctxt "dev_update_found_label"
msgid "Update found:"
msgstr "Mise à jour trouvée :"

#. Developer page (Windows): prefix of the update check result on a development build; the version follows.
msgctxt "dev_update_newest_release_is"
msgid "Newest release is"
msgstr "La dernière version publiée est"

#. Developer page (Windows): inside the parentheses after 'No update', before the newest release's version.
msgctxt "dev_update_newest_seen"
msgid "newest release seen:"
msgstr "dernière version vue :"

#. Developer page, and the line under Linux Settings > Check for updates: update check result when there is no stable release.
msgctxt "dev_update_no_releases"
msgid "No stable release has been published yet."
msgstr "Aucune version stable n’a encore été publiée."

#. Developer page (Windows): update check result on the newest release; the version details follow in parentheses.
msgctxt "dev_update_none"
msgid "No update: this build is current"
msgstr "Pas de mise à jour : cette version est à jour"

#. Developer page, and the line under Linux Settings > Check for updates: update check result on the newest release. {version} is the release version.
msgctxt "dev_update_up_to_date"
msgid "Up to date. Newest release: v{}"
msgstr "À jour. Dernière version : v{}"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): uplink gate control label.
msgctxt "dev_uplink_gate"
msgid "Uplink silence gate"
msgstr "Filtre de silence montant"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'uplink gate' control.
msgctxt "dev_uplink_gate_detail"
msgid "How long the whole tunnel may be silent before provider verdicts are held as inadmissible. 0 convicts as before"
msgstr "Combien de temps tout le tunnel peut rester silencieux avant que les verdicts sur les fournisseurs soient retenus comme irrecevables. 0 condamne comme avant"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Uplink silence gate' setting.
msgctxt "dev_uplink_silence_gate"
msgid "Uplink silence gate"
msgstr "Filtre de silence montant"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Uplink silence gate' setting.
msgctxt "dev_uplink_silence_gate_detail"
msgid "How long the whole tunnel may be silent before provider verdicts are held as inadmissible, in ms. 0 convicts as before"
msgstr "Combien de temps tout le tunnel peut rester silencieux avant que les verdicts sur les fournisseurs soient retenus comme irrecevables, en ms. 0 condamne comme avant"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): verdicts held control label.
msgctxt "dev_verdicts_held"
msgid "Verdicts held"
msgstr "Verdicts retenus"

#. Developer page: label of the 'Verdicts held' measurement (desktop wording of dev_verdicts_held).
msgctxt "dev_verdicts_held_desktop"
msgid "Verdicts held"
msgstr "Verdicts retenus"

#. Developer page: the explanation under the 'Verdicts held' measurement (desktop wording).
msgctxt "dev_verdicts_held_desktop_detail"
msgid "Convictions withheld because this machine's own uplink, not the provider, was silent (uplink / transport)"
msgstr "Condamnations retenues parce que la liaison montante de cet ordinateur, et non le fournisseur, était silencieuse (liaison montante / transport)"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'verdicts held' control.
msgctxt "dev_verdicts_held_detail"
msgid "Convictions withheld because the phone's own uplink, not the provider, was silent (uplink / transport)"
msgstr "Condamnations retenues parce que la liaison montante du téléphone lui-même, et non le fournisseur, était silencieuse (liaison montante / transport)"

#. Developer tools screen: formatted value readout for 'verdicts held'.
msgctxt "dev_verdicts_held_value"
msgid "{0} / {1}"
msgstr "{0} / {1}"

#. Developer tools screen (reliability surface): worst loss control label.
msgctxt "dev_worst_loss"
msgid "Worst single failure"
msgstr "Pire panne unique"

#. Developer tools screen: explanatory subtext under the 'worst loss' control.
msgctxt "dev_worst_loss_detail"
msgid "The one the user actually feels"
msgstr "Celle que l’utilisateur ressent vraiment"

#. Developer tools screen: formatted value readout for 'worst loss'.
msgctxt "dev_worst_loss_value"
msgid "{} connections"
msgstr "Connexions : {}"

#. Developer page: value of the worst single failure, {count} connections.
msgctxt "dev_worst_single_failure_value"
msgid "{} connections"
msgstr "Connexions : {}"

#. Developer tools screen: developer.
msgctxt "developer"
msgid "Developer"
msgstr "Développeur"

#. Developer tools screen: developer description.
msgctxt "developer_description"
msgid "Tools for diagnosing connection freezes. These act on the live connection."
msgstr "Outils pour diagnostiquer les blocages de connexion. Ils agissent sur la connexion en cours."

#. Developer tools screen: developer disconnected.
msgctxt "developer_disconnected"
msgid "Connect to use these tools."
msgstr "Connectez-vous pour utiliser ces outils."

#. device
msgctxt "device"
msgid "Device"
msgstr "Appareil"

#. Status label shown when this device can be discovered by peers on the network.
msgctxt "device_discoverable"
msgid "This device is discoverable"
msgstr "Cet appareil est détectable"

#. Status label shown when this device can be discovered by peers, with the device's visible name. The argument is the device name.
msgctxt "device_discoverable_as"
msgid "This device is discoverable as {}"
msgstr "Cet appareil est détectable sous le nom {}"

#. Used in Main/Account/Settings/SettingsView.swift.
msgctxt "device_name"
msgid "Device name"
msgstr "Nom de l'appareil"

#. device
msgctxt "device_name_label"
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Nom"

#. Snackbar shown after the device name is saved. Used in Main/Account/Settings/SettingsView.swift.
msgctxt "device_name_updated"
msgid "Device name updated"
msgstr "Nom de l'appareil mis à jour"

#. Hint shown when the device is not discoverable because provide mode is off.
msgctxt "device_not_discoverable"
msgid "Enable provide mode to make this device discoverable"
msgstr "Activez le mode de fourniture pour rendre cet appareil détectable"

#. device
msgctxt "device_spec_label"
msgid "Spec"
msgstr "Modèle"

#. Provider list group title for devices
msgctxt "devices"
msgid "Devices"
msgstr "Appareils"

#. macOS folder-access panel button that grants the app access to the Applications folder for the update.
msgctxt "direct_update_allow"
msgid "Allow"
msgstr "Autoriser"

#. macOS folder-access panel message when installing an update: the user selects the Applications folder to grant access. Keep "Allow" consistent with the panel's button.
msgctxt "direct_update_allow_applications"
msgid "To install the update, allow URnetwork to replace itself in the Applications folder. Select Applications and click Allow."
msgstr "Pour installer la mise à jour, autorisez URnetwork à se remplacer dans le dossier Applications. Sélectionnez Applications et cliquez sur Autoriser."

#. macOS Settings > Software update status when a newer release exists. {version} is its version.
msgctxt "direct_update_available"
msgid "Update available: {}"
msgstr "Mise à jour disponible : {}"

#. macOS Settings > Software update button that checks now.
msgctxt "direct_update_check"
msgid "Check for updates"
msgstr "Rechercher des mises à jour"

#. macOS Settings > Software update error. {detail} is a short technical reason (often English, from the system).
msgctxt "direct_update_check_failed"
msgid "Could not check for updates: {}"
msgstr "Impossible de rechercher des mises à jour : {}"

#. macOS Settings > Software update status while checking.
msgctxt "direct_update_checking"
msgid "Checking for updates…"
msgstr "Recherche de mises à jour…"

#. macOS Settings > Software update error: the downloaded file failed its integrity check and was deleted.
msgctxt "direct_update_checksum_failed"
msgid "The download did not match the release checksum and was discarded."
msgstr "Le téléchargement ne correspondait pas à la somme de contrôle de la version et a été supprimé."

#. macOS Settings > Software update status on a development build, which never updates itself. {version} is the newest release version.
msgctxt "direct_update_development_build"
msgid "Development build; the newest release is {}."
msgstr "Version de développement ; la dernière version est {}."

#. macOS Settings > Software update error. {detail} is a short technical reason.
msgctxt "direct_update_download_failed"
msgid "The download failed: {}"
msgstr "Le téléchargement a échoué : {}"

#. macOS Settings > Software update status while the release downloads. {version} is its version.
msgctxt "direct_update_downloading_version"
msgid "Downloading {}…"
msgstr "Téléchargement de {}…"

#. macOS Settings > Software update button that downloads, verifies and installs the update.
msgctxt "direct_update_install"
msgid "Install update"
msgstr "Installer la mise à jour"

#. macOS Settings > Software update error. {detail} is a short technical reason.
msgctxt "direct_update_install_failed"
msgid "The update could not be installed: {}"
msgstr "La mise à jour n’a pas pu être installée : {}"

#. macOS Settings > Software update status while the verified update is installed.
msgctxt "direct_update_installing"
msgid "Installing the update…"
msgstr "Installation de la mise à jour…"

#. macOS Settings > Software update: when updates were last checked. {when} is a relative date, for example "5 minutes ago" or "yesterday".
msgctxt "direct_update_last_checked"
msgid "Last checked {}"
msgstr "Dernière vérification : {}"

#. macOS Settings > Software update status when the app could not replace itself. {version} is the downloaded release's version.
msgctxt "direct_update_manual_install"
msgid "{} was downloaded and verified. Drag the new URnetwork into the Applications folder, then open it from there."
msgstr "{} a été téléchargée et vérifiée. Faites glisser le nouvel URnetwork dans le dossier Applications, puis ouvrez-le depuis cet emplacement."

#. macOS Settings > Software update status before the first check.
msgctxt "direct_update_not_checked"
msgid "Updates have not been checked yet."
msgstr "Aucune recherche de mises à jour n’a encore été effectuée."

#. macOS Settings > Software update status while the app restarts on the new version.
msgctxt "direct_update_relaunching"
msgid "Relaunching URnetwork…"
msgstr "Redémarrage d’URnetwork…"

#. macOS Settings: title of the section that checks for and installs app updates (direct-download app).
msgctxt "direct_update_section_title"
msgid "Software update"
msgstr "Mise à jour de logiciels"

#. macOS Settings > Software update button that reveals the downloaded update in Finder (the macOS file manager).
msgctxt "direct_update_show_in_finder"
msgid "Show in Finder"
msgstr "Afficher dans le Finder"

#. macOS Settings > Software update error when the downloaded app's code signature did not check out. {detail} is a short technical reason.
msgctxt "direct_update_signature_rejected"
msgid "The update was rejected: {}"
msgstr "La mise à jour a été refusée : {}"

#. macOS Settings > Software update error. {detail} is a short technical reason.
msgctxt "direct_update_unpack_failed"
msgid "The download could not be unpacked: {}"
msgstr "Le téléchargement n’a pas pu être décompressé : {}"

#. macOS Settings > Software update error when the newest release has no file this app can install. {version} is the release version; {reason} is a short technical reason.
msgctxt "direct_update_unusable_release"
msgid "Release {0} cannot be installed by the app ({1})."
msgstr "La version {0} ne peut pas être installée par l’application ({1})."

#. macOS Settings > Software update status when no newer release exists.
msgctxt "direct_update_up_to_date"
msgid "URnetwork is up to date."
msgstr "URnetwork est à jour."

#. Hint under the Ignore battery optimizations row in builds that can ask for the exemption directly. Once the exemption is on, tapping the row opens Android's system battery optimization list, which by default shows only apps that are not optimized; the quoted labels are Android's own labels for the list filter and the per-app choice.
msgctxt "disable_ignore_battery_settings_hint"
msgid "To turn this off, tap the switch to open Android's battery optimization list, switch the filter to “All apps”, then choose URnetwork and “Optimize”."
msgstr "Pour désactiver cette option, touchez l’interrupteur pour ouvrir la liste d’optimisation de la batterie d’Android, réglez le filtre sur « Toutes les applications », puis choisissez URnetwork et « Optimiser »."

#. Disconnect VPN button text
msgctxt "disconnect"
msgid "Disconnect"
msgstr "Déconnecter"

#. Used in Shared/Intents/DisconnectIntent.swift.
msgctxt "disconnect_urnetwork_vpn"
msgid "Disconnect URnetwork VPN"
msgstr "Déconnecter URnetwork VPN"

#. Connection status shown on the connect panel and in the tray tooltip when the tunnel is down. The counterpart of the `connected` key.
msgctxt "disconnected"
msgid "Disconnected"
msgstr "Déconnecté"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "dismiss"
msgid "Dismiss"
msgstr "Fermer"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "display_network_on_leaderboard"
msgid "Display network on leaderboard"
msgstr "Afficher le réseau dans le classement"

#. iOS and macOS DNS settings: note that DNS configuration profiles installed on the device don't apply inside the VPN tunnel; the DNS chosen on this screen does.
msgctxt "dns_apple_profiles_note"
msgid "DNS profiles installed on this device don't apply while connected. The DNS chosen here is used instead."
msgstr "Les profils DNS installés sur cet appareil ne s'appliquent pas pendant la connexion. C'est le DNS choisi ici qui est utilisé."

#. DNS settings: how many DNS lookups the selected adblock provider has blocked since the device connected. Counted on the device only and reset at each connect. {count} is the number, {provider} the selected preset's name (dns_preset_name_*, for example AdGuard Ad Blocking), inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_blocked_count"
msgid "{0} lookup blocked by {1} this connection"
msgid_plural "{0} lookups blocked by {1} this connection"
msgstr[0] "{0} requête bloquée par {1} pendant cette connexion"
msgstr[1] "{0} requêtes bloquées par {1} pendant cette connexion"

#. DNS settings: note under the blocked lookups count. Some ways an adblock provider answers a block can't be recognized, so the count is a minimum.
msgctxt "dns_blocked_count_floor_note"
msgid "Some blocks aren't counted, so the real number may be higher."
msgstr "Certains blocages ne sont pas comptés : le nombre réel peut donc être plus élevé."

#. Connect drawer and DNS settings: label of the toggle for URnetwork's own ad and tracker blocker, which works on the device beside any DNS choice. It is named as URnetwork's own so it isn't mistaken for the adblock providers in "Block ads and trackers".
msgctxt "dns_builtin_blocker_label"
msgid "URnetwork ad blocker"
msgstr "Bloqueur de publicités d'URnetwork"

#. Connect drawer and DNS settings: line under the URnetwork ad blocker toggle. It can stay on with any DNS choice, an adblock provider that blocks ads included, and it checks each name before the chosen DNS is asked.
msgctxt "dns_builtin_blocker_note"
msgid "URnetwork's own blocker. It works with any DNS choice and checks each name first."
msgstr "Le bloqueur intégré d'URnetwork. Il fonctionne avec n'importe quel choix de DNS et vérifie chaque nom en premier."

#. DNS settings, Custom: note that a filtering DNS server added beside URnetwork's default servers doesn't filter, because each lookup takes the fastest answer, usually an unfiltered one.
msgctxt "dns_custom_mix_note"
msgid "Mixing a filtering server with the default servers doesn't filter: the fastest answer wins."
msgstr "Mélanger un serveur filtrant avec les serveurs par défaut ne filtre pas : la réponse la plus rapide l'emporte."

#. dns settings
msgctxt "dns_default_not_applied"
msgid "The default safe settings are not applied"
msgstr "Les paramètres sûrs par défaut ne sont pas appliqués"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: heading of the group of adblock providers that block malware and phishing but not ads (Cloudflare, DNS4EU, Quad9). It sits below "Block ads and trackers" and reads like it.
msgctxt "dns_group_block_malware"
msgid "Block malware"
msgstr "Bloquer les logiciels malveillants"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: heading of the group of the adblock providers' family filters, which block adult sites and similar content (some of them also block ads).
msgctxt "dns_group_family"
msgid "Family"
msgstr "Famille"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: heading of the group for people with their own account at an adblock provider (AdGuard DNS, Control D, NextDNS). Choosing one asks for the account's profile ID, so the adblock provider applies the person's own filters.
msgctxt "dns_group_my_account"
msgid "Use my account"
msgstr "Utiliser mon compte"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: heading of the group of the adblock providers' picks that resolve every name and block nothing.
msgctxt "dns_group_no_filtering"
msgid "No filtering"
msgstr "Sans filtrage"

#. A label displayed in a row of a custom dns settings.
msgctxt "dns_over_https"
msgid "DNS over HTTPS"
msgstr "DNS via HTTPS"

#. DNS settings, Use my account: help about the adblock provider's block response setting. URnetwork treats a REFUSED answer as a failing adblock provider, so blocks must be answered with zero IP (0.0.0.0, the adblock providers' default) or NXDOMAIN. 0.0.0.0, NXDOMAIN and REFUSED are technical values: keep them as they are. {provider} is the adblock provider's name, inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_block_response"
msgid "In {}, keep the block response at zero IP (0.0.0.0, the default) or NXDOMAIN. REFUSED and other responses look like an outage."
msgstr "Dans {}, gardez la réponse de blocage sur IP nulle (0.0.0.0, par défaut) ou NXDOMAIN. REFUSED et les autres réponses ressemblent à une panne."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: link that opens the adblock provider's dashboard, for example under "Saved, but we can't confirm this profile". {provider} is the adblock provider's name, inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_dashboard_link"
msgid "Open your {} dashboard"
msgstr "Ouvrir votre tableau de bord {}"

#. DNS settings, Use my account: shown under the profile ID field when the AdGuard DNS device ID has the wrong format. {provider} is AdGuard DNS and {example} an example ID such as 1a2b3c4d, both inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_format_adguard"
msgid "{0} device IDs are 8 characters: digits and the letters a to f, like {1}."
msgstr "Les ID d'appareil {0} comptent 8 caractères : des chiffres et les lettres a à f, par exemple {1}."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: shown under the profile ID field when the Control D resolver ID has the wrong format. {provider} is Control D and {example} an example ID such as abcd1234, both inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_format_controld"
msgid "{0} resolver IDs use only letters and digits, like {1}."
msgstr "Les ID de résolveur {0} ne contiennent que des lettres et des chiffres, par exemple {1}."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: shown under the profile ID field when the NextDNS ID has the wrong format. {provider} is NextDNS and {example} an example ID such as abc123, both inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_format_nextdns"
msgid "{0} IDs are 6 characters: digits and the letters a to f, like {1}."
msgstr "Les ID {0} comptent 6 caractères : des chiffres et les lettres a à f, par exemple {1}."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: label of the field where the person enters the ID of their profile at the adblock provider, or pastes the DNS address the adblock provider's dashboard shows (a DNS over HTTPS URL or a Private DNS hostname).
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_label"
msgid "Profile ID or DNS address"
msgstr "ID de profil ou adresse DNS"

#. DNS settings, Use my account: adblock provider dashboards suggest linking your IP address to your account. Through URnetwork, lookups come from the VPN exit's address, which belongs to someone else, so the app uses only the ID and doesn't offer linking.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_linked_ip_note"
msgid "No need to link an IP address in your dashboard: through URnetwork, your lookups come from an address that isn't yours. Your ID is enough."
msgstr "Inutile d'associer une adresse IP dans votre tableau de bord : avec URnetwork, vos requêtes proviennent d'une adresse qui n'est pas la vôtre. Votre ID suffit."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: free-plan note under the profile ID field for AdGuard DNS. What happens at the limit is not documented, so the note states only the limit. {provider} is AdGuard DNS, inserted as is. The sdk names this key for the preset.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_quota_adguard"
msgid "{}'s free plan is limited to 300,000 requests a month."
msgstr "L'offre gratuite de {} est limitée à 300 000 requêtes par mois."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: free-plan note under the profile ID field for NextDNS, which answers without filtering once the free monthly queries are used up. {provider} is NextDNS, inserted as is. The sdk names this key for the preset.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_quota_nextdns"
msgid "{}'s free plan stops filtering after 300,000 queries a month."
msgstr "L'offre gratuite de {} cesse de filtrer après 300 000 requêtes par mois."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: help under the profile ID field for AdGuard DNS. {provider} is AdGuard DNS, inserted as is. Each device's page in the AdGuard DNS dashboard shows its device ID and DNS addresses.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_where_adguard"
msgid "Find it on your device's page in your {} dashboard."
msgstr "Vous le trouverez sur la page de votre appareil dans votre tableau de bord {}."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: help under the profile ID field for Control D. {provider} is Control D, inserted as is. "Show Resolvers" is the button's name in Control D's English dashboard, so it stays in English; an endpoint is what Control D calls a device or profile you connect.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_where_controld"
msgid "In your {} dashboard, choose Show Resolvers on your endpoint."
msgstr "Dans votre tableau de bord {}, choisissez Show Resolvers sur votre endpoint."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: help under the profile ID field for NextDNS. {provider} is NextDNS, inserted as is. "Setup" is the name of the page in the NextDNS dashboard, so it stays in English.
msgctxt "dns_personal_id_where_nextdns"
msgid "Find it on the Setup page of your {} account."
msgstr "Vous le trouverez sur la page Setup de votre compte {}."

#. dns settings
msgctxt "dns_pill_default"
msgid "The default safe settings are not applied"
msgstr "Les paramètres sûrs par défaut ne sont pas appliqués"

#. DNS status pill shown when the default safe DNS settings are not applied.
msgctxt "dns_pill_defaults"
msgid "The default safe settings are not applied"
msgstr "Les paramètres sûrs par défaut ne sont pas appliqués"

#. dns settings
msgctxt "dns_pill_recommended"
msgid "There are unapplied recommended settings for {}"
msgstr "Des paramètres recommandés pour {} ne sont pas appliqués"

#. DNS settings: footnote. A new DNS choice applies to new lookups at once, but apps keep answers they already have for up to about a minute.
msgctxt "dns_preset_apply_note"
msgid "Changes apply to new lookups right away. Apps may keep earlier answers for about a minute."
msgstr "Les modifications s'appliquent tout de suite aux nouvelles requêtes. Les applications peuvent garder les réponses précédentes environ une minute."

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks. Used for AdGuard DNS Family in "Family": it also forces safe search on search engines. The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_ads_adult_safe_search"
msgid "Blocks ads, trackers and adult sites, and turns on safe search"
msgstr "Bloque les publicités, les traqueurs et les sites pour adultes, et active la recherche sécurisée"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks. Used for Control D in "Block ads and trackers". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_ads_malware"
msgid "Blocks ads, trackers and malware"
msgstr "Bloque les publicités, les traqueurs et les logiciels malveillants"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks. Used for Control D Family in "Family". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_ads_malware_adult_drugs"
msgid "Blocks ads, trackers, malware, adult sites and drugs"
msgstr "Bloque les publicités, les traqueurs, les logiciels malveillants, les sites pour adultes et la drogue"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks. Used for DNS4EU in "Block ads and trackers". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_ads_malware_phishing"
msgid "Blocks ads, trackers, malware and phishing"
msgstr "Bloque les publicités, les traqueurs, les logiciels malveillants et l'hameçonnage"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks. Used for AdGuard DNS in "Block ads and trackers". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_ads_phishing"
msgid "Blocks ads, trackers and phishing"
msgstr "Bloque les publicités, les traqueurs et l'hameçonnage"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks, and that it doesn't block ads. Used for DNS4EU's child protection in "Family". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_child"
msgid "Blocks malware, adult sites, gambling, drugs and violence, not ads"
msgstr "Bloque les logiciels malveillants, les sites pour adultes, les jeux d'argent, la drogue et la violence, pas les publicités"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks. Used for DNS4EU's child protection with ad blocking in "Family". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_child_ads"
msgid "Blocks ads, trackers, malware, adult sites, gambling, drugs and violence"
msgstr "Bloque les publicités, les traqueurs, les logiciels malveillants, les sites pour adultes, les jeux d'argent, la drogue et la violence"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under DNS4EU in "No filtering". It does no protective filtering, but the domains courts order blocked stay blocked on every DNS4EU resolver. The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_court_orders"
msgid "Blocks only what courts order it to block"
msgstr "Ne bloque que ce que les tribunaux ordonnent de bloquer"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks, and that it doesn't block ads. Used for Cloudflare in "Block malware". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_malware"
msgid "Blocks malware, not ads"
msgstr "Bloque les logiciels malveillants, pas les publicités"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks, and that it doesn't block ads. Used for Cloudflare Family in "Family". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_malware_adult"
msgid "Blocks malware and adult sites, not ads"
msgstr "Bloque les logiciels malveillants et les sites pour adultes, pas les publicités"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name that says what it blocks, and that it doesn't block ads. Used for DNS4EU and Quad9 in "Block malware". The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_malware_phishing"
msgid "Blocks malware and phishing, not ads"
msgstr "Bloque les logiciels malveillants et l'hameçonnage, pas les publicités"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under an adblock provider's name in "No filtering" (AdGuard DNS, Cloudflare, Control D): the adblock provider resolves every name and blocks nothing. The adblock provider's name is shown above it, not in this string.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_nothing"
msgid "Blocks nothing"
msgstr "Ne bloque rien"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under each adblock provider in "Use my account". {provider} is the adblock provider's name (AdGuard DNS, Control D or NextDNS), inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_preset_copy_personal"
msgid "Uses the filters you set up in your {} account"
msgstr "Utilise les filtres définis dans votre compte {}"

#. DNS settings: disclosure under the selected adblock provider, above the Privacy policy and Help links. The adblock provider receives the names looked up while connected, from the VPN exit's address, never the person's own IP address. {provider} is the adblock provider's name (for example AdGuard DNS), inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_preset_disclosure"
msgid "Your DNS lookups go to {} through the tunnel, so it never sees your IP address. Its privacy policy applies."
msgstr "Vos requêtes DNS passent par le tunnel jusqu'à {}, qui ne voit donc jamais votre adresse IP. Sa politique de confidentialité s'applique."

#. DNS settings and connect drawer: notice after an app update removed the preset the person had selected. The app switched to URnetwork's own DNS, which doesn't filter. {provider} is the removed preset's name (dns_preset_name_*, for example AdGuard Family), inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_preset_dropped"
msgid "{} is no longer available. You're using URnetwork DNS, so lookups aren't filtered."
msgstr "{} n'est plus disponible. Vous utilisez le DNS d'URnetwork : les requêtes ne sont donc pas filtrées."

#. DNS settings: button on the notice of a removed adblock provider that opens the adblock provider list. "Preset" means one of the adblock providers listed on the screen.
msgctxt "dns_preset_dropped_choose"
msgid "Choose another preset"
msgstr "Choisir un autre préréglage"

#. DNS settings: button on the notice of a removed adblock provider that opens the Custom editor, where the person can enter the adblock provider's addresses themselves. It names the "Custom" pick, so it uses that pick's exact word.
msgctxt "dns_preset_dropped_custom"
msgid "Enter it yourself under Custom"
msgstr "Le saisir vous-même dans Personnalisé"

#. DNS settings, Use my account: error id the sdk returns when the profile ID doesn't have the adblock provider's format. The adblock provider's own format line is shown with it.
msgctxt "dns_preset_error_personal_id_invalid"
msgid "This ID isn't in the right format."
msgstr "Cet ID n'est pas au bon format."

#. DNS settings: error id the sdk returns when a profile ID is given for a DNS preset that doesn't take one. "Preset" means one of the adblock providers listed on the screen.
msgctxt "dns_preset_error_personal_id_not_accepted"
msgid "This preset doesn't use a profile ID."
msgstr "Ce préréglage n'utilise pas d'ID de profil."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: error id the sdk returns when the pasted DNS address or hostname belongs to another adblock provider in the list. "Adblock provider" is what the app calls these DNS companies (AdGuard, Control D, Quad9, Cloudflare, DNS4EU, NextDNS): say it in full both times, never with the word the app uses for URnetwork's providers, which are the bandwidth providers.
msgctxt "dns_preset_error_personal_id_other_provider"
msgid "This address belongs to another adblock provider. Choose that adblock provider instead."
msgstr "Cette adresse appartient à un autre fournisseur de blocage des publicités. Choisissez plutôt ce fournisseur de blocage des publicités."

#. DNS settings, Use my account: error id the sdk returns when the profile ID field is empty.
msgctxt "dns_preset_error_personal_id_required"
msgid "Enter your profile ID."
msgstr "Saisissez votre ID de profil."

#. DNS settings: error id the sdk returns when a DNS preset is no longer in the app's catalog. "Preset" means one of the adblock providers listed on the screen.
msgctxt "dns_preset_error_unknown"
msgid "This preset isn't available. Choose another one."
msgstr "Ce préréglage n'est pas disponible. Choisissez-en un autre."

#. DNS settings: note beside the "Fast DNS on connect" toggle while an adblock provider is selected. While the tunnel connects, lookups go to URnetwork's own DNS, so the adblock provider never sees the person's own address, but those lookups aren't filtered. {provider} is the selected preset's name (dns_preset_name_*, for example AdGuard Family), inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_preset_fast_dns_note"
msgid "While connecting, lookups use URnetwork DNS, so {} doesn't filter them."
msgstr "Pendant la connexion, les requêtes passent par le DNS d'URnetwork : {} ne les filtre donc pas."

#. DNS settings: link under the selected adblock provider, beside "Privacy policy", that opens the adblock provider's help page.
msgctxt "dns_preset_help_link"
msgid "Help"
msgstr "Aide"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: which country's law the adblock provider operates under. {jurisdiction} comes from the app's adblock provider catalog in English (for example Cyprus or Switzerland) and is inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_preset_jurisdiction"
msgid "Jurisdiction: {}"
msgstr "Juridiction : {}"

#. DNS settings: the name of an adblock provider's preset in "Block ads and trackers", which blocks ads and trackers. Shown alone as the preset's label on the DNS screen, and inserted as is wherever the selected preset is named, as in "DNS: AdGuard Ad Blocking" and "AdGuard Ad Blocking isn't answering", so it reads as a short name that works on its own and inside a sentence. {provider} is the adblock provider's short name, inserted as is (for example AdGuard); keep it first, so the presets of a group stay in alphabetical order.
msgctxt "dns_preset_name_ad_blocking"
msgid "{} Ad Blocking"
msgstr "{} Blocage des publicités"

#. DNS settings: the name of DNS4EU's child protection preset in "Family", which blocks malware, adult sites, gambling, drugs and violence and doesn't block ads. Next to it is the same protection with ads blocked (dns_preset_name_child_ads). Shown alone as the preset's label on the DNS screen, and inserted as is wherever the selected preset is named, as in "DNS: DNS4EU Child" and "DNS4EU Child isn't answering", so it reads as a short name that works on its own and inside a sentence. {provider} is the adblock provider's short name, inserted as is (for example DNS4EU); keep it first, so the presets of a group stay in alphabetical order.
msgctxt "dns_preset_name_child"
msgid "{} Child"
msgstr "{} Enfants"

#. DNS settings: the name of DNS4EU's child protection preset that also blocks ads and trackers, in "Family". "no ads" means the person sees no ads, because they are blocked. Next to it is the same protection without ad blocking (dns_preset_name_child). Shown alone as the preset's label on the DNS screen, and inserted as is wherever the selected preset is named, as in "DNS: DNS4EU Child, no ads" and "DNS4EU Child, no ads isn't answering", so it reads as a short name that works on its own and inside a sentence. {provider} is the adblock provider's short name, inserted as is (for example DNS4EU); keep it first, so the presets of a group stay in alphabetical order.
msgctxt "dns_preset_name_child_ads"
msgid "{} Child, no ads"
msgstr "{} Enfants, sans publicité"

#. DNS settings: the name of an adblock provider's preset in "Family", which blocks adult sites and, for some adblock providers, ads. Shown alone as the preset's label on the DNS screen, and inserted as is wherever the selected preset is named, as in "DNS: AdGuard Family" and "AdGuard Family isn't answering", so it reads as a short name that works on its own and inside a sentence. {provider} is the adblock provider's short name, inserted as is (for example AdGuard); keep it first, so the presets of a group stay in alphabetical order.
msgctxt "dns_preset_name_family"
msgid "{} Family"
msgstr "{} Famille"

#. DNS settings: the name of an adblock provider's preset in "Block malware", which blocks malware and doesn't block ads. Shown alone as the preset's label on the DNS screen, and inserted as is wherever the selected preset is named, as in "DNS: Quad9 Malware Blocking" and "Quad9 Malware Blocking isn't answering", so it reads as a short name that works on its own and inside a sentence. {provider} is the adblock provider's short name, inserted as is (for example Quad9); keep it first, so the presets of a group stay in alphabetical order.
msgctxt "dns_preset_name_malware_blocking"
msgid "{} Malware Blocking"
msgstr "{} Blocage des logiciels malveillants"

#. DNS settings: the name of an adblock provider's preset in "No filtering", which blocks nothing. Shown alone as the preset's label on the DNS screen, and inserted as is wherever the selected preset is named, as in "DNS: Cloudflare No Filtering" and "Cloudflare No Filtering isn't answering", so it reads as a short name that works on its own and inside a sentence. {provider} is the adblock provider's short name, inserted as is (for example Cloudflare); keep it first, so the presets of a group stay in alphabetical order.
msgctxt "dns_preset_name_no_filtering"
msgid "{} No Filtering"
msgstr "{} Sans filtrage"

#. DNS settings: the name of an adblock provider's preset in "Use my account", which uses the filters the person set up in their own account there. It never includes the account's ID. Shown alone as the preset's label on the DNS screen, and inserted as is wherever the selected preset is named, as in "DNS: NextDNS Personal" and "NextDNS Personal isn't answering", so it reads as a short name that works on its own and inside a sentence. {provider} is the adblock provider's short name, inserted as is (for example NextDNS); keep it first, so the presets of a group stay in alphabetical order.
msgctxt "dns_preset_name_personal"
msgid "{} Personal"
msgstr "{} Personnel"

#. DNS settings: link under the selected adblock provider that opens the adblock provider's privacy policy.
msgctxt "dns_preset_privacy_link"
msgid "Privacy policy"
msgstr "Politique de confidentialité"

#. Android connect screen: line added to the strict Private DNS notice while an adblock provider is selected, since Android's Private DNS sends lookups to its own server instead. {provider} is the selected preset's name (dns_preset_name_*, for example AdGuard Family), inserted as is. Private DNS is Android's own setting, named as in Android.
msgctxt "dns_private_dns_overrides_preset"
msgid "Private DNS overrides your DNS choice ({})."
msgstr "Le DNS privé remplace votre choix de DNS ({})."

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the pick that opens the advanced editor, where the person enters their own DNS over HTTPS URLs and DNS servers. Other strings send the reader to this pick by name ("Enter it yourself under Custom"), so they use the same word.
msgctxt "dns_provider_custom"
msgid "Custom"
msgstr "Personnalisé"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under "Custom" that says what it holds.
msgctxt "dns_provider_custom_copy"
msgid "Your own DNS over HTTPS URLs and DNS servers"
msgstr "Vos propres URL DNS via HTTPS et serveurs DNS"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the first pick, URnetwork's own encrypted DNS through the tunnel, which every app uses by default. URnetwork is the product name.
msgctxt "dns_provider_default"
msgid "URnetwork (default)"
msgstr "URnetwork (par défaut)"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the line under "URnetwork (default)" that says what it does: names are resolved over encrypted DNS inside the VPN tunnel, and nothing is blocked.
msgctxt "dns_provider_default_copy"
msgid "Encrypted DNS through the tunnel, with no filtering"
msgstr "DNS chiffré à travers le tunnel, sans filtrage"

#. DNS settings, adblock provider picker: the last pick, shown only while the exit's country has a recommended set of plain DNS servers that work better there. It is never selected automatically. {country} is the exit country's name, inserted as is. Unencrypted means the DNS lookups are sent without encryption.
msgctxt "dns_provider_regional"
msgid "Regional ({}), unencrypted"
msgstr "Régional ({}), non chiffré"

#. dns settings
msgctxt "dns_recommendation_message"
msgid "The strongest security rules are known not to work in {}. There are less secure recommended DNS settings that work better."
msgstr "{} — les règles de sécurité les plus strictes n'y fonctionnent pas. Des paramètres DNS recommandés, moins sécurisés, fonctionnent mieux."

#. A message displayed when the dns settings are unavailable.
msgctxt "dns_settings_unavailable"
msgid "DNS settings unavailable"
msgstr "Paramètres DNS indisponibles"

#. DNS settings and connect drawer: button beside an adblock provider's status that opens the location picker, since an adblock provider can be blocked or unreachable from some exit locations.
msgctxt "dns_status_change_location"
msgid "Change location"
msgstr "Changer d'emplacement"

#. DNS settings and connect drawer: status line when an adblock provider from "No filtering" isn't answering, so URnetwork's own DNS answers until it does. {provider} is the selected preset's name (dns_preset_name_*, for example Cloudflare No Filtering), inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_status_fallback"
msgid "{} isn't answering. Using URnetwork DNS."
msgstr "{} ne répond pas. Le DNS d'URnetwork est utilisé."

#. DNS settings and connect drawer: status line when an adblock provider that blocks ads isn't answering from the current exit, so URnetwork's own DNS answers for now and ads aren't blocked. It switches back on its own when the adblock provider answers. {provider} is the selected preset's name (dns_preset_name_*, for example AdGuard Ad Blocking), inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_status_paused"
msgid "Ad blocking paused: {} isn't answering"
msgstr "Blocage des publicités en pause : {} ne répond pas"

#. DNS settings: line under "Ad blocking paused: … isn't answering". "it" is the adblock provider named in that line.
msgctxt "dns_status_paused_detail"
msgid "Using URnetwork DNS until it answers. Ad blocking comes back on its own."
msgstr "Le DNS d'URnetwork prend le relais jusqu'à ce que le fournisseur de blocage des publicités réponde. Le blocage des publicités reprendra tout seul."

#. DNS settings and connect drawer: status line while the selected preset answers normally, and the summary row of a selected preset. {provider} is the preset's name (dns_preset_name_*, for example AdGuard Family), inserted as is; the name already says what the preset does.
msgctxt "dns_status_provider"
msgid "DNS: {}"
msgstr "DNS : {}"

#. DNS settings and connect drawer: status line when an adblock provider's family, malware-blocking or personal pick isn't answering. To keep its filtering, URnetwork doesn't switch to other DNS, so sites may not load until the adblock provider answers or the person picks "Use URnetwork DNS". {provider} is the selected preset's name (dns_preset_name_*, for example AdGuard Family), inserted as is.
msgctxt "dns_status_unreachable"
msgid "{} isn't answering"
msgstr "{} ne répond pas"

#. DNS settings: line under "… isn't answering" for an adblock provider's family, malware-blocking or personal pick. "it" is the adblock provider named in that line.
msgctxt "dns_status_unreachable_detail"
msgid "To keep filtering on, URnetwork doesn't switch DNS for you. Sites may not load until it answers."
msgstr "Pour garder le filtrage actif, URnetwork ne change pas de DNS de lui-même. Les sites peuvent ne pas se charger tant que le fournisseur de blocage des publicités ne répond pas."

#. DNS settings and connect drawer: button beside the status of an adblock provider that isn't answering. It switches back to URnetwork's own DNS, the default, in one tap.
msgctxt "dns_status_use_default"
msgid "Use URnetwork DNS"
msgstr "Utiliser le DNS d'URnetwork"

#. Connect drawer, DNS card: summary row while the person's own servers are selected under "Custom", all of them encrypted.
msgctxt "dns_summary_custom"
msgid "DNS: Custom"
msgstr "DNS : Personnalisé"

#. Connect drawer, DNS card: summary row while the person's own servers are selected under "Custom" and some lookups are sent without encryption (plain DNS is on).
msgctxt "dns_summary_custom_unencrypted"
msgid "DNS: Custom (unencrypted)"
msgstr "DNS : Personnalisé (non chiffré)"

#. Connect drawer, DNS card: summary row while URnetwork's own DNS, the default, is selected. URnetwork is the product name.
msgctxt "dns_summary_default"
msgid "DNS: URnetwork"
msgstr "DNS : URnetwork"

#. Connect drawer, DNS card: summary row while the regional pick is selected: plain DNS servers recommended for the exit's country, which send lookups without encryption.
msgctxt "dns_summary_regional"
msgid "DNS: Regional (unencrypted)"
msgstr "DNS : Régional (non chiffré)"

#. dns settings
msgctxt "dns_unapplied_recommended"
msgid "There are unapplied recommended settings for {}"
msgstr "Des paramètres recommandés pour {} ne sont pas appliqués"

#. DNS settings, Use my account: AdGuard DNS fails every lookup for a device ID it can't read. {provider} is AdGuard DNS, inserted as is. "Device ID" is AdGuard DNS's name for the ID.
msgctxt "dns_verify_malformed_adguard"
msgid "{} rejected this device ID"
msgstr "{} a refusé cet ID d'appareil"

