#. Status line under the Open a port on my router switch once the router forwards the extender's ports. The first argument is the ports, such as TCP 443, UDP 443, UDP 4053 (an arrow joins a router port to the device's, as TCP 40443→443); the second is how the router was asked: PCP, NAT-PMP or UPnP. Neither is translated.
msgctxt "extender_port_mapping_mapped"
msgid "Your router forwards {0} ({1})."
msgstr "Votre routeur redirige {0} ({1})."

#. Status line under the Open a port on my router switch while the router's first answer is awaited.
msgctxt "extender_port_mapping_mapping"
msgid "Asking your router…"
msgstr "Interrogation de votre routeur…"

#. Status line under the Open a port on my router switch: the device has a public address, so the router is not asked to open anything.
msgctxt "extender_port_mapping_not_needed"
msgid "Not needed: this device has a public address."
msgstr "Inutile : cet appareil a une adresse publique."

#. Extender status when the operator revoked this device's extender key.
msgctxt "extender_revoked"
msgid "Revoked by the operator"
msgstr "Révoqué par l’opérateur"

#. Secondary text under the Extender setting: what turning it on does, and the ports the extender listens on.
msgctxt "extender_setting_description"
msgid "While you are providing, this device also relays for people whose access to the network is blocked, on TCP and UDP 443 and UDP 4053."
msgstr "Pendant que vous fournissez, cet appareil relaie aussi pour les personnes dont l’accès au réseau est bloqué, en TCP et UDP 443 et en UDP 4053."

#. Extender status while the role is starting and there is no outcome yet: the carriers are binding, or the first activation is in flight.
msgctxt "extender_setting_up"
msgid "Setting up"
msgstr "Configuration"

#. Title of the extender settings form under account > Extenders.
msgctxt "extender_settings"
msgid "Extender settings"
msgstr "Paramètres de l’extendeur"

#. Note on iOS after saving extender settings: the packet tunnel extension reads them at its next start.
msgctxt "extender_settings_next_connect"
msgid "The tunnel uses new extender settings the next time it connects."
msgstr "Le tunnel utilisera les nouveaux paramètres de l’extendeur à sa prochaine connexion."

#. Confirmation after the extender settings are saved.
msgctxt "extender_settings_saved"
msgid "Extender settings saved"
msgstr "Paramètres de l’extendeur enregistrés"

#. Title of the switch under the Extender setting that lets people on lag.dev run latency and speed tests to this device. lag.dev is a website name and stays as written.
msgctxt "extender_speed_tests"
msgid "lag.dev speed tests"
msgstr "Tests de débit lag.dev"

#. Secondary text under the lag.dev speed tests switch: what turning it on allows, and its cost. lag.dev is a website name and stays as written.
msgctxt "extender_speed_tests_description"
msgid "Let people testing their connection on lag.dev measure latency, download and upload to this device. Tests use some of your bandwidth while they run."
msgstr "Autorisez les personnes qui testent leur connexion sur lag.dev à mesurer la latence, le téléchargement et l'envoi vers cet appareil. Les tests utilisent une partie de votre bande passante pendant leur exécution."

#. Extender status when the setting is on and the device is providing, but the role could not start in this network space: no extender directory or no identity. The argument is the reason.
msgctxt "extender_start_failed"
msgid "Could not start: {}"
msgstr "Démarrage impossible : {}"

#. Title of the section that shows statistics about the extender, directly above the provider statistics section.
msgctxt "extender_statistics"
msgid "Extender statistics"
msgstr "Statistiques de l’extendeur"

#. Extender status when TCP port 443, the one port the extender requires, cannot be bound, usually because another program (often another provider on the same computer) holds it. The extender stays off and tries the port again every few minutes on its own, so this is not the user's mistake: keep the tone calm. The argument is the bind error.
msgctxt "extender_tcp_unavailable"
msgid "TCP port 443 is in use by another program. Trying again every few minutes: {}"
msgstr "Le port TCP 443 est utilisé par un autre programme. Nouvelle tentative toutes les quelques minutes : {}"

#. Title of the extenders panel in the connect drawer and of the Extenders section under account.
msgctxt "extenders"
msgid "Extenders"
msgstr "Extendeurs"

#. The extender panel count: extenders carrying a live connection now, of every usable extender the app knows.
msgctxt "extenders_active_of_reserve"
msgid "{0} of {1}"
msgstr "{0} sur {1}"

#. Shown in the account Extenders section when there is no signed-in device to manage extenders with.
msgctxt "extenders_no_session"
msgid "Sign in and connect to manage extenders."
msgstr "Connectez-vous à votre compte et au réseau pour gérer les extendeurs."

#. Confirmation after the extenders were reset (Extenders section under account).
msgctxt "extenders_reset_done"
msgid "Extenders reset"
msgstr "Extendeurs réinitialisés"

#. Browser extension popup, out-of-balance alert: a button that opens ur.io's data packs (ur.io/buy-data) in a new tab. Short.
msgctxt "extension_buy_data"
msgid "Buy data"
msgstr "Acheter des données"

#. Browser extension popup, under the button: a connect failed and the server gave no reason of its own (when it gives one, the popup shows that instead).
msgctxt "extension_connect_failed"
msgid "Failed to connect. Check your account."
msgstr "Échec de la connexion. Vérifiez votre compte."

#. Browser extension popup, out-of-balance alert for a Pro account at its plan's data, while the extension holds the browser's traffic: ur.io's data packs (the Buy data button) can't load through URnetwork until the user disconnects, and nothing disconnects for them. Disconnect is the button above this line; name it by its own label (the disconnect key). The free plan's counterpart is insufficient_balance_disconnect_first.
msgctxt "extension_data_limit_disconnect_first"
msgid "To buy data, press Disconnect first. Payment can't get through until you do."
msgstr "Pour acheter des données, choisissez d’abord « Déconnecter ». Le paiement ne peut pas aboutir avant cela."

#. Browser extension popup, the IP line at its top, while the popup asks which IP address the browser's requests leave from. IP is the IP address.
msgctxt "extension_ip_checking"
msgid "Checking IP…"
msgstr "Vérification de l’IP…"

#. Browser extension popup, the IP line at its top, when the check of which IP address the browser's requests leave from failed. Short.
msgctxt "extension_ip_unavailable"
msgid "IP unavailable"
msgstr "IP indisponible"

#. Browser extension popup, subtitle under the Kill switch toggle while it is on: if the proxy fails, the browser's traffic stops instead of going out without URnetwork. Short.
msgctxt "extension_kill_switch_blocks_on_failure"
msgid "Blocks traffic on failure"
msgstr "Bloque le trafic en cas de panne"

#. Browser extension popup, subtitle under the Kill switch toggle while it is off (its default): if the proxy fails, the browser's traffic can go out without URnetwork. Short.
msgctxt "extension_kill_switch_may_leak_on_failure"
msgid "Traffic may leak on failure"
msgstr "Le trafic peut fuiter en cas de panne"

#. Browser extension popup, under the reason a location change failed: the change did not happen, and the browser stays connected through the proxy and the location it had before.
msgctxt "extension_location_unchanged"
msgid "The browser is still connected at the previous location."
msgstr "Le navigateur reste connecté à l’emplacement précédent."

#. Browser extension popup, under the settings toggles, beside the Turn on alerts button (extension_turn_on_alerts): what the alerts are. Once the user allows it, the browser shows one notification when the account's data runs out, also while the popup is closed.
msgctxt "extension_out_of_data_alerts_note"
msgid "Get a notification when your data runs out."
msgstr "Recevez une notification quand vos données sont épuisées."

#. Browser extension popup, out-of-balance alert, and the body of the browser notification for it: the account has no data left, and the extension keeps its proxy set whatever the kill switch says, so pages fail rather than load without URnetwork, until the free refresh, an upgrade or a data pack makes data available, or the user presses Disconnect. The ur.io counterpart is site_out_of_data_browser_held, without its kill switch clause.
msgctxt "extension_out_of_data_held"
msgid "Pages won't load in this browser until data is available or you disconnect."
msgstr "Les pages ne se chargeront pas dans ce navigateur tant que des données ne sont pas disponibles ou que vous ne vous déconnectez pas."

#. Browser extension popup, note under the button: the browser is set to the extension's proxy, but the popup's own IP check found three times running that requests do not leave through URnetwork.
msgctxt "extension_proxy_active_network_unreachable"
msgid "Proxy active but network unreachable."
msgstr "Proxy actif, mais réseau injoignable."

#. Browser extension popup, under the Connect button (status Disconnected): the proxy failed three health checks in a row with the kill switch off, so the extension took its proxy setting off, and the browser went back to its own connection (direct, or the proxy its own settings name). Keep URnetwork as is.
msgctxt "extension_proxy_fell_back"
msgid "The proxy stopped answering, so the extension turned it off. This browser connects without URnetwork until you connect again."
msgstr "Le proxy ne répondait plus, l’extension l’a donc désactivé. Ce navigateur se connecte sans URnetwork jusqu’à ce que vous vous reconnectiez."

#. Browser extension popup, under the button while the status line reads Another extension controls the proxy (extension_status_other_extension). Turning the other extension off is done in the browser's extension settings. Keep URnetwork as is.
msgctxt "extension_proxy_other_extension"
msgid "Another extension controls this browser's proxy settings, so URnetwork can't connect. Turn that extension off to use URnetwork."
msgstr "Une autre extension contrôle les paramètres de proxy de ce navigateur, URnetwork ne peut donc pas se connecter. Désactivez cette extension pour utiliser URnetwork."

#. Browser extension popup, under the button while the status line reads Proxy managed by policy (extension_status_proxy_policy). Keep URnetwork as is.
msgctxt "extension_proxy_policy"
msgid "This browser's proxy settings are managed by policy, so URnetwork can't connect."
msgstr "Les paramètres de proxy de ce navigateur sont gérés par une règle, URnetwork ne peut donc pas se connecter."

#. Browser extension popup, under the Disconnect button while the status line reads Proxy not answering (extension_status_proxy_not_answering): why pages don't load. Translate kill switch as the kill_switch key does.
msgctxt "extension_proxy_unreachable_kill_switch"
msgid "The proxy is not answering. The kill switch keeps the browser offline until it does."
msgstr "Le proxy ne répond pas. Le kill switch maintient le navigateur hors ligne jusqu’à ce que le proxy réponde."

#. Browser extension popup, under the Kill switch or the location sync toggle when saving a change failed: the toggle went back to its previous state.
msgctxt "extension_setting_not_saved"
msgid "The setting couldn't be saved, so it didn't change. Try again."
msgstr "Le paramètre n’a pas pu être enregistré, il n’a donc pas été modifié. Réessayez."

#. Browser extension popup, status line at its foot: another browser extension holds the browser's proxy setting, and the browser gives it priority over URnetwork, so URnetwork is not connected. Short.
msgctxt "extension_status_other_extension"
msgid "Another extension controls the proxy"
msgstr "Une autre extension contrôle le proxy"

#. Browser extension popup, status line at its foot: the kill switch keeps the extension's proxy set although the proxy failed three health checks in a row, so this browser is offline until the proxy answers or the user disconnects. Short.
msgctxt "extension_status_proxy_not_answering"
msgid "Proxy not answering"
msgstr "Le proxy ne répond pas"

#. Browser extension popup, status line at its foot: the browser's proxy settings are fixed by policy (set by an administrator or an organization), so no extension can set them and URnetwork is not connected. Short; use the word the browser itself uses for its managed settings in the language.
msgctxt "extension_status_proxy_policy"
msgid "Proxy managed by policy"
msgstr "Proxy géré par une règle"

#. Browser extension popup: a small button, shown while the browser has not let the extension show notifications, that asks the browser for that permission. With it, the extension shows one browser notification when the account runs out of data; without it, the popup's alert and a ! on the toolbar icon show it. It sits under the settings toggles beside extension_out_of_data_alerts_note, and in the out-of-data alert beside Get Pro and Buy data. Short.
msgctxt "extension_turn_on_alerts"
msgid "Turn on alerts"
msgstr "Activer les alertes"

#. Used in Shared/Intents/ConnectIntent.swift.
msgctxt "failed_to_connect"
msgid "Failed to connect"
msgstr "Échec de la connexion"

#. Used in Shared/Intents/DisconnectIntent.swift.
msgctxt "failed_to_connect_urnetwork"
msgid "Failed to connect URnetwork"
msgstr "Échec de la connexion à URnetwork"

