msgstr "Fourniture (en pause)"

#. Shown when the post-checkout confirmation poll gives up (2 minutes) without the server confirming the subscription. The purchase is still likely to land later; the background poll and the next launch pick it up. On apple: the delayed phase of PurchaseSuccessView and the MainView snackbar.
msgctxt "purchase_confirmation_timeout"
msgid "We couldn't confirm your purchase yet. If you completed checkout, your plan will update automatically in a few minutes — there's no need to buy again."
msgstr "Nous n'avons pas encore pu confirmer votre achat. Si vous avez terminé le paiement, votre plan sera mis à jour automatiquement dans quelques minutes — inutile d'acheter à nouveau."

#. Error dialog body when the server's verify answer for a Play purchase is terminal `invalid` — the proof will never verify (unknown token, disallowed product, canceled before completing). The purchase is still acknowledged with Play so a real charge is not auto-refunded; this dialog is how the failure reaches the user instead of a silent nothing (android google/PlanViewModel.kt report path).
msgctxt "purchase_could_not_be_verified"
msgid "This purchase could not be verified with Google Play, so it can't be applied to your account. If you were charged and your plan doesn't update, please contact support."
msgstr "Cet achat n’a pas pu être vérifié auprès de Google Play, il ne peut donc pas être appliqué à votre compte. Si vous avez été débité et que votre forfait ne se met pas à jour, contactez l’assistance."

#. Mac App Store alert body under purchase_disconnect_notice_title. The app reconnects the VPN by itself after the purchase; "it" is the VPN. Until then the user's internet traffic does not go through the VPN: the kill switch is off whenever this alert shows.
msgctxt "purchase_disconnect_notice_message"
msgid "URnetwork reconnects it afterward. Until it does, your internet traffic won't go through the VPN."
msgstr "URnetwork le reconnectera ensuite. D’ici là, votre trafic Internet ne passera pas par le VPN."

#. Mac App Store build's alert title, shown when the user starts a purchase while a VPN connection is requested and the kill switch is off, before the app disconnects the VPN for the purchase. The alert's buttons are Disconnect and Cancel. With the kill switch on, purchase_kill_switch_notice_title shows instead.
msgctxt "purchase_disconnect_notice_title"
msgid "Disconnect the VPN for this purchase?"
msgstr "Déconnecter le VPN pour cet achat ?"

#. Restore-purchases outcome: an entitlement for the current network was found; the confirmation poll now bridges the gap until the server credits it (Shared/ViewModels/AppStoreSubscriptionManager.swift).
msgctxt "purchase_found_confirming_your_plan"
msgid "Purchase found. Confirming your plan — it will update automatically."
msgstr "Achat trouvé. Confirmation de votre forfait — il se mettra à jour automatiquement."

#. Mac App Store alert body under purchase_kill_switch_notice_title. In "while it's disconnected", "it" is the VPN; in "turn it back on", "it" is the kill switch, which the user may turn back on after the purchase. Keep App Store and VPN as they are. Name the kill switch by the label of its setting (the kill_switch key).
msgctxt "purchase_kill_switch_notice_message"
msgid "App Store purchases need the VPN disconnected, and while it's disconnected, the kill switch blocks your internet traffic. Turn off the kill switch, then try again. You can turn it back on afterward."
msgstr "Les achats sur l’App Store nécessitent que le VPN soit déconnecté, et tant qu’il l’est, le Kill switch bloque votre trafic Internet. Désactivez le Kill switch, puis réessayez. Vous pourrez le réactiver ensuite."

#. Mac App Store build's alert title, shown in place of purchase_disconnect_notice_title when the user starts a purchase while the kill switch is on. An App Store purchase there needs the VPN disconnected, and with the kill switch on the internet traffic is blocked while the VPN is disconnected, so nothing is bought until the user turns the kill switch off. The alert's one button is Got it. Name the kill switch by the label of its setting (the kill_switch key).
msgctxt "purchase_kill_switch_notice_title"
msgid "Turn off the kill switch to buy"
msgstr "Désactivez le Kill switch pour acheter"

#. Upgrade: the overlay shown while a store purchase waits for approval. Keep UR Pro (the plan's name) unchanged.
msgctxt "purchase_pending_body"
msgid "Your purchase is waiting for approval. UR Pro will turn on by itself once it goes through — there's no need to buy again."
msgstr "Votre achat est en attente d’approbation. UR Pro s’activera tout seul dès qu’il sera validé — inutile d’acheter à nouveau."

